{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed","id":942281,"title":"Exalted: 2nd ed vs 3rd ed","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-02T15:40:45-07:00","id":942281,"title":"Exalted: 2nd ed vs 3rd ed","content":"OK, I know how trolling-like such thread looks like. Althogh, let me explain.<br /> I really like the concept of Exalted - the chacters, who were born and nutried to be cool, and who can change the world on so many levels (not just kick some monster's ass), but the system always seems to be too complex and overload for me. I hoped that 3rd edition will be better, but after I read, it's look like new edition fix some bugs just to add another. Also, it will take God-knows-how-many-years before every Exalt-splut will have a rulebook. So, should I try it or it's better to finaly investigate 2nd edition.I mean forChronicles of Darkness, after 2nd edition my reaction was &quot;Hell, finaly this crap start to work as it should!!!&quot;.Will it be the same reaction for 3rd ed of Exalt?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T17:03:36-07:00","id":942324,"title":"","content":"Significant improvements in 3e, from my perspective [incomplete list, just things that pop into my head]:<br /> <br /> Internal scaling for Solar charms. Solars actually feel like they have room in all abilities, but especially noncombat ones, between dabbler and master [Stealth in 2e core book was four charms. FOUR. Dodge was about as long.] Also, they don't immediately [or in a lot of/most cases, ever] just jump to &quot;you never need to roll again unless you're opposing another Solaroid&quot;, unlike 2e.<br /> <br /> Combat. Combat in 2e was very much rocket tag. Every single attack was targetting your health levels, which in theory makes for gripping exciting combat but in practice means the only winning strategy [barring regeneration Lunars or the like] was just to never get hit, which meant combat was a long series of ineffectual swats depleting an invisible mote counter until one side ran out of motes and abruptly died from the next attack. 3e's split between initiative and health level attacks, withering and decisive damage, allows for far better combats that feel like you're making ground, like you can actually tell the swing of the battle beyond your own mote count. Also, the former perfect defenses are properly priced from the beginning, so they're there primarily as a &quot;oh shit&quot; button and a &quot;I don't die to chump-slaying death beams&quot; instead of &quot;spam cheaper perfect, win&quot;. Overall 3e combat is more engaging and doesn't have the perpetual feel of &quot;I could deploy my ultimate combo, BUT it'd probably be perfected and leave me at a disadvantage, so I guess it's back to jabbing&quot;.<br /> <br /> Martial Arts: Martial Arts in 2e felt like kind of a waste; if you were a Solar pursuing them, outside of Solar Hero Style and its' infinite Solar-tiered expansions [which would become Brawl charms], they were [barring standout combos or individual charms that were obscenely overpowered compared to the rest] inferior to what you could get for being a Solar. So they felt neat, but hamstrung. Mastery keyword means that martial arts can be used by Solars to stand shoulder to shoulder with native charms [in their narrower focused areas] while not making them a One True Build for everyone else. Which leads to...<br /> <br /> Non-Solar optimism: While we don't know too much about non-Solars, we can make some inferences, chief among them the relative disparity between basic Martial Arts charms, Mastery, and Terrestrial. And in my estimation, the disparity between Mastery and Terrestrial is about what I'd have expected to exist between Solar and Celestial in 2e; if martial arts are any indication at all, non-Solars will be a more significant player mechanically, making a confrontation with an experienced Lunar or Sidereal much less of a foregone conclusion and pointless waste of time to play out, and making being the non-Solar in a group far less of a &quot;Scrappy Doo&quot; position.<br /> <br /> Social system: Oh my god it actually works beyond &quot;OBEY ME *hammers until out of willpower, forces mind control*&quot;, and is cool and encourages actual interaction and figuring out of hooks to ingratiate yourself with the NPC. It feels better, it's more fun in play, and mostly pleasing in a thematic rather than utilitarian sense, the &quot;scene-long perfect&quot; of joining battle is gone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","user":"Meianno Yuurei","date":". 08-02-2016, 08:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":16}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T17:21:20-07:00","id":942339,"title":"","content":"Yeah, if it's still too complex for a lot of people's tastes, I can understand completely. But I'd say Ex3 fixes far more than it breaks (I haven't really found anything outright broken yet, to be honest.. I'm still deciding if I like how crafting was set up, for instance, but it's not broken or buggy or anything), and a lot of the in-depth mechanical systems are actually quite fun and interesting if you're willing to use them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9749-andrew-d","name":"Andrew D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T17:31:32-07:00","id":942341,"title":"","content":"I am by no means the best candidate to tell you what to play. Only you can decide that really. I have however been playing Exalted since 1st edition. My thoughts are as follows:<br /> <br /> 1E: Was a good game all around. It's lore/narrative are really what drew me to Exalted all those years ago. It had it's fair share of mechanical issues as well (Lunar's were broke even then). I feel it's problems though were known well enough that simple house rules could keep the game going. However, that's just my opinion and I'm sure many others disagreed. Regardless, good games almost always develop enough cracks that a 2.0 reboot is required. So I wasn't upset when 2E was announced as a project.<br /> <br /> 2E: Well it was a bit rocky even at the start. Even in the beginning the &quot;paranoia combat&quot; became a known issue. What really killed it though was that each supplement added more mechanics that were either broken to begin with, or were broken by later supplements. A lot of this was laid at the feet of different writers each having conflicting points of view, and very little play test and oversight of what was being sent to the press. The end result being a game that was very unforgiving and punishing to new players, and required a lot of ST mediation to keep from breaking even with experienced players. I believe the majority of us weren't surprised or terribly upset with the announcement of 3E.<br /> <br /> 3E: So far, I'm enjoying 3E a lot. I really like the new combat system, as well as all the sorcery/artifact widgets. The few lore changes have been quite inspiring as well. It has some issues to work out, but nothing I've seen so far is so broken that it's un-fixable. Even the Craft system can be greatly improved with a few tweaks as several people have displayed in other posts. So I'm going to stay positive about the few wrinkles we've found. Who knows, maybe the next few supplements will add to the existing rules and iron out those pesky wrinkles we've identified!<br /> <br /> TLDR:<br /> <br /> 1E: great 1st gen game with some well documented cracks<br /> 2E: so bloated and broke that entire books could be dedicated to errata and not fix it<br /> 3E: new and refreshing, but Exalted is a huge setting and future products will either make or break this edition","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2103,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","user":"TalosX","date":". 08-02-2016, 08:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T18:51:14-07:00","id":942388,"title":"","content":"My advice? Play it. Like, get a group together and play it. Even if it's something as simple as &quot;Okay, you're some bad dudes and the Princess was kidnapped by Ninjas&quot;, so that you guys pick up the system a bit at a time.<br /> <br /> Because let me let you in on a little secret. Those things that LOOK uncertain and finicky when you're looking at them in the book? A LOT of them become less of an issue when you actually sit down and play it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T18:57:19-07:00","id":942393,"title":"","content":"Ex3 is a beast of a system. There is no way around that. If your group normally errs on the system-light side of gaming, Ex3 probably isn't your cup of tea.<br /> <br /> If you like crunch-heavy games, then you will find the core systems make sense after a few sessions with it. They aren't more complex than Pathfinder, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T19:45:29-07:00","id":942424,"title":"","content":"If you do try the 3E system and like it, but are stopped by the lack of your favorite splat, there are fan conversions on this forum (and presumably other fora) for Lunars, Sidereals, and Dragon-Blooded. Also Abyssals and Alchemicals, but I don't know if they're finished. And Green Sun Princes and Dragon Kings, which aren't finished AFAIK.<br /> <br /> There are also 2 rewrites of the Solar Charms to be easier to read or play differently, and are various thaumaturgy, MA, and Sorcery alterations around here too. And people are converting elementals, demons, and spells from 2E. You can ask us for links if there's a particular homebrew you need/want.<br /> <br /> I don't know if anyone is converting Necromancy, Nocturnals, Raksha, Jadeborn, or Modern Charms.<br /> <br /> Actual canon DBs will be published soonish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 08-03-2016, 12:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T20:30:43-07:00","id":942446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=942424#post942424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actual canon DBs will be published soonish.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dragonblood published &quot;soonish&quot;... being a relative term for us all! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As Erinys has said, there's quite a lot of fan generated content already being passed around. Also, while there's spots of negativity and the occasional bickering going on, I can honestly say I have yet to see someone post asking for help and not get several responses within a few days time. A lot of people that visit these forums are always willing to help out ST or players if you ask!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2103-talosx","name":"TalosX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"588"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-02T20:40:34-07:00","id":942452,"title":"","content":"If you're only interested in playing Alchemicals, 2nd edition is fine. Otherwise, ease yourself into Ex3. Set up your fights so they only require Withering and Decisive attacks at first, then add movement and gambits. Limit your social influence to persuade and read intentions at first before expanding. If someone in the group wants crafting, tell them to start with a Craft that allows them to just do something simple to keep their hands busy while the group is just hanging around. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T00:37:13-07:00","id":942553,"title":"","content":"If you don't like &quot;complex, overload-y systems&quot;, neither edition is probably going to be your jam. Exalted has always been a really complex system that expects its ST to do a HELL of a lot of work. You might want to consider something friendlier. I sure know that while I've <i>played </i>Exalted, you wouldn't catch me dead STing it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T01:23:50-07:00","id":942568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=942424#post942424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you do try the 3E system and like it, but are stopped by the lack of your favorite splat, there are fan conversions on this forum (and presumably other fora) for Lunars, Sidereals, and Dragon-Blooded. Also Abyssals and Alchemicals, but I don't know if they're finished. And Green Sun Princes and Dragon Kings, which aren't finished AFAIK.</div> </div> </div> </div> Link, please?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=942553#post942553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you don't like &quot;complex, overload-y systems&quot;, neither edition is probably going to be your jam. Exalted has always been a really complex system that expects its ST to do a HELL of a lot of work. You might want to consider something friendlier. I sure know that while I've <i>played </i>Exalted, you wouldn't catch me dead STing it!</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I'm ready to work with complex systems and I like them (i.g. lack of crunch is my mane problem with Dresden Files RPG). I like 2.0 Chronicles of Darkness. But among complex systems I prefer more understandable one))</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T02:09:30-07:00","id":942580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=942568#post942568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Link, please?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I'm ready to work with complex systems and I like them (i.g. lack of crunch is my mane problem with Dresden Files RPG). I like 2.0 Chronicles of Darkness. But among complex systems I prefer more understandable one))</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Then I'll repeat. Give it a shot.<br /> <br /> Some starter advice: If you're STing with your party, maybe start them on smaller battles. Nothing they need to burst out all their Charms for, just something to ease them into the combat first, and THEN add the Charms.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/>