v> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-460#post-4027054\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/data/svg/20/1/1794123741/logo_icon.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-460#post-4027054\" target=\"_blank\"> General Exalted Thread </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-460#post-4027054\" target=\"_blank\"> https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-460#post-4027054 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Mechanically she's a hellstrider, and Keris will probably drink five doses of chalcanth to get the exotic ingredients to make her simply because it's easier that way. In-setting, she's a decidedly inhuman akuma-child who's probably about the level of a sublimatus - that is to say, \"better than a... </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/772458-the-gaian-dance-a-3e-lunars-writeup\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/772458-the-gaian-dance-a-3e-lunars-writeup\"> The Gaian Dance - A 3E Lunars Writeup - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/772458-the-gaian-dance-a-3e-lunars-writeup\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/772458-the-gaian-dance-a-3e-lunars-writeup </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Yes, you read this correctly. I'm working on a fan writeup for one of my few favorite splats, prior to the release of the book itself. I'm hoping that this will be </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/718165-3rd-ed-lunar-fan-conversion\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/718165-3rd-ed-lunar-fan-conversion\"> 3rd ed Lunar fan conversion - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/718165-3rd-ed-lunar-fan-conversion\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/718165-3rd-ed-lunar-fan-conversion </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Here's my 3rd ed Lunar conversion. Obviously this isn't finished: not like there's been all that much time so far, I did most of this today and yesterday, though </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Green Sun Princes:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Qp1rHy1Tm-jQBWEtPIj1G4JSol9xYFCRBEnZZKNm1K4\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Qp1rHy1Tm-jQBWEtPIj1G4JSol9xYFCRBEnZZKNm1K4\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Qp1rHy1Tm-jQBWEtPIj1G4JSol9xYFCRBEnZZKNm1K4\" target=\"_blank\"> https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Qp1rHy1Tm-jQBWEtPIj1G4JSol9xYFCRBEnZZKNm1K4 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/76242-the-infernals-thread-2e-2-5e\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/76242-the-infernals-thread-2e-2-5e\"> The Infernals Thread (2E / 2.5E) - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/76242-the-infernals-thread-2e-2-5e\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/76242-the-infernals-thread-2e-2-5e </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> So much useful discussion and inspiration material disappeared with the old forums, so I feel there's worth in retreading some old ground. Here's a thread for discussing the old Infernals. A few topics to get us started: 1) What are some suggested Infernal builds? I know there's Killfuck Soulshitter the </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/782596-infernal-3e-beta-conversion?p=801594#post801594\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/782596-infernal-3e-beta-conversion?p=801594#post801594\"> Infernal 3e Beta Conversion - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/782596-infernal-3e-beta-conversion?p=801594#post801594\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/782596-infernal-3e-beta-conversion?p=801594#post801594 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> So as my boredom continues, I have decided to try and do Infernals. Infernals are a bit trickier than Alchemicals for several reasons: While I could cheat and </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/815113-ex3-raziere-s-infernal-homebrew\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/815113-ex3-raziere-s-infernal-homebrew\"> [Ex3] Raziere's Infernal Homebrew - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/815113-ex3-raziere-s-infernal-homebrew\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/815113-ex3-raziere-s-infernal-homebrew </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Converting Infernals to 3e: First let us address the most important problem here: the lack of skills. If you want to a pure Infernals conversion with no skills </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-6\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/data/svg/20/1/1794123741/logo_icon.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-6\" target=\"_blank\"> General Exalted Thread </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-6\" target=\"_blank\"> https://forums.sufficientvelocity.com/threads/general-exalted-thread.44/page-6 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Honestly, I would just compress the current five Dawn abilities down into Melee, Ranged and Command, and have done with it. </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/929481-infernals-what-hell-has-claimed-peach\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/929481-infernals-what-hell-has-claimed-peach\"> Infernals: What Hell Has Claimed [PEACH] - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/929481-infernals-what-hell-has-claimed-peach\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/929481-infernals-what-hell-has-claimed-peach </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> So I sat down and wrote some charms based on the earlier discussion about Infernal characters. So far, I've got some resistance done and not a lot else, but figured </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Dragon Kings:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\"> Ex3 Dragon Kings homebrew - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I wrote up rules for everyone's favourite dinosaur monsters. The document contains all 15 Paths, and should have everything you need to play a Dragon King, but I </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> God-Blooded from Celestial Exalted:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/749025-homebrew-children-of-celestial-exalts\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...lestial-exalts</a></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T09:51:37-07:00","id":942772,"title":"","content":"Something that worked for my group, and quite a few others from what I've read, is starting with a mortals game. Have your players roll up heroic mortals and play through the game for several sessions doing combat, social influence, battle groups, crafting (if anyone wants to), sorcery, etc. without any charms or mote pools.<br /> <br /> If everyone has a solid understanding of the game, it's a lot easier to later incorporate charms, because all they do is break the rules of one of those systems in their own individual way. They'll have a much better sense of what it means to, say, &quot;double post-soak damage dice&quot; if they've already done some combat. I think it's possible to take in all of the rules, from the base systems through all of the charms, just by reading them, but it's probably a lot easier and smoother to build off of a foundation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9749-andrew-d","name":"Andrew D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T09:58:48-07:00","id":942778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=942568#post942568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Link, please?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Here are the Lunars and the easier-to-read Solar rewrite:","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T10:23:13-07:00","id":942794,"title":"","content":"With respect to Irked, I'd recommend not going straight to the charm rewrite (which removes some charms and changes some of their effects, not just writing them in fewer words) unless you actually have problems with the charms in the book.<br /> <br /> Same for any house rules, really. It's one thing to add charms that don't exist yet, so you can throw in some Lunar or Dragon-Blooded or Sidereal NPCs, but you might miss out if you don't take the time to see if you like the rules as written in actual play before incorporating someone's homebrew. If there's one thing that browsing this forum should make pretty clear, it's that - even when complaints are presented as being objective or somehow universal - not everyone agrees that charms are incoherent or crafting sucks or dice tricks have no place in an RPG, or whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9749-andrew-d","name":"Andrew D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T11:17:49-07:00","id":942825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lashet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed#post942281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&lt;snip&gt;the system always seems to be too complex and overload for me. I hoped that 3rd edition will be better, but after I read, it's look like new edition fix some bugs just to add another. Also, it will take God-knows-how-many-years before every Exalt-splut will have a rulebook. So, should I try it or it's better to finaly investigate 2nd edition.I mean forChronicles of Darkness, after 2nd edition my reaction was &quot;Hell, finaly this crap start to work as it should!!!&quot;.Will it be the same reaction for 3rd ed of Exalt?</div> </div> </div> </div>I love the 3rd edition (3E) setting. It feels like the early days of 1st edition (1E). Also, it appears to be the most stable mechanical rule set for Exalted ever published. But when I introduced it to my players, showed them the combat mechanics (along with the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/724173-requesting-exalted-combat-tutorial-example\">combat tutorial thread</a> I started) and the Craft minigame, they unanimously voted against upgrading from the edition we are playing. :/ They didn't even make it to any of the other minigames like social combat.<br /> <br /> The thing about 2E was that there were some serious mechanical flaws. Some struggled with the rule flaws more than others. But it was serious enough that there was a major update to the rules referred to as the 2.5 edition, the Scroll of Errata. That's the system that we are using. If you're like me and my players who love a great story but really struggle with really complex mechanical systems, 2.5E might be the system for you. It's complex but appears to be less so than 3E. Although I would recommend running 2.5E games with 3E's setting by throwing out the vast majority of the magitech science-fiction material.<br /> <br /> If you do decide to give 3E a try I highly recommend that <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/724173-requesting-exalted-combat-tutorial-example\">combat tutorial thread</a>.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-03T13:38:00-07:00","id":942960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Andrew D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=942794#post942794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With respect to Irked, I'd recommend not going straight to the charm rewrite (which removes some charms and changes some of their effects, not just writing them in fewer words) unless you actually have problems with the charms in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not quite true! I never actually <i>removed</i> Charms; I just tagged that some of them as having been removed in my game. The rewrites of those Charms were still physically present, just... disrecommended.<br /> <br /> And there's a clean version now that cuts those tags! The edit of a month ago or so brings it basically in line with the core, with the remaining changes clearly footnoted. (Most of those are things like &quot;The original is Permanent/Permanent; this version is Reflexive/Instant, but practically speaking, works exactly the same way.&quot;)<br /> <br /> (It remains true that, for some of 'em, I had to guess which of several meanings the original rules intended, if we want to call that a change.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> not everyone agrees that charms are incoherent or crafting sucks or dice tricks have no place in an RPG, or whatever. </div> </div> </div>Ehh. There are some objectively-true critiques; &quot;There are no rules for generic counterattacks of the form offered by Crane Style,&quot; for instance, is factually true. There are several other topics where that's also the case, before we get into things like, &quot;<i>As written</i>, this effect seems to do such-and-such, but is that really the intent?&quot;<br /> <br /> (Hi there, Increasing Strength Exercise + Iron Whirlwind Attack.)<br /> <br /> I should stress that I'm playing and enjoying 3e, but also that (as evidenced) I've put large portions of the rules in a blender in order to facilitate that state.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 08-03-2016, 04:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-04T01:09:36-07:00","id":943480,"title":"","content":"Erinis, Irked - thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4950-lashet","name":"Lashet","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"281"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T02:57:16-07:00","id":946833,"title":"","content":"Sorry, I didn't read everyone's posts (it's hard to go through them all using JAWS) but I wanted to give my opinion.<br /> <br /> I think you should go with 2E. The way it sounds, I think the abundance of material for 2nd edition is something you'll really like. And it's AMAZINGLY well written. Both the Abyssal and Infernal books are just a delight to read. The only issue, I feel, 2nd has is in System, but as a Storyteller game, system always takes a back seat to story in my book. Also, if you're an experienced ST, you won't have any trouble making rules calls on the fly if an issue comes up. I LOVE OP and WW, but when it comes to clear rules, well...they're not as clear as other game systems. Which, imo, is fine, as their fluff MORE than makes up for it. <br /> <br /> 3E has an issue I've been venting about (and catching a lot of flack for) for a bit now in that I feel it's not as supported as it used to be. For any number of reasons which I'm sure lots of other people have already mentioned and made excuses for. I don't care really, I just want more books. The thing about 3E is the system is...well, it's a work of art, imo. It's great. I really wish I had the time and inclination to adapt it's system to the 2E books. I don't though. I'm Visually Impaired and it's hard enough to run games without having to do that. Or make up all the Charms for all the other Exalts or all those great Artifacts or any number of other things.<br /> <br /> So, my vote, in the end, is go with 2nd Edition for now. Then, in 10 years when the number of books for 3E gets to a decent number, switch.<br /> <br /> As a side note, I've been asking myself the same question. Should I go 2nd or 3rd? I'm starting up a new Exalted game and this line being my all time favorite, it's been weighing heavily upon me. I decided to go with 2nd for all the reasons I gave you. Want to have Abyssal enemies with clearly written powers now? 2nd Ed then. If you don't mind making up almost everything as you go, outside of maybe 8 Charms, for each Exalt type, go for 3E.<br /> <br /> I would like to AGAIN say: I LOVE 3E. The System is amazing. Love those new MA. The new Caste Rules.<br /> <br /> ...just find it...lacking...in everything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1101-blindst","name":"blindST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T04:06:10-07:00","id":946849,"title":"","content":"What's better - a small (admittedly too small) amount of material for a great system, or a wealth of material for a so-bad-it's-not-really-playable system?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T04:17:07-07:00","id":946852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=946849#post946849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's better - a small (admittedly too small) amount of material for a great system, or a wealth of material for a so-bad-it's-not-really-playable system?</div> </div> </div> </div>The system isn't unplayable. It very playable. I can say this with absolute certainty as I ran it for many years. If it was unplayable, there would be no way to play it. Just saying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1101-blindst","name":"blindST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T04:39:24-07:00","id":946860,"title":"","content":"People do play FATAL. Doesn't mean it's playable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T04:54:14-07:00","id":946866,"title":"","content":"Paranoia combat of exalted 2e is frankly my main issue overall and the fact that the infernals were gutted with the latest errata since a lot of their charms were built with the minimum damage essence rules in mind now beside going devil tigers, they are pretty much the dorks of the celestial exalts, ending up not doing much.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2127-eltacolibre","name":"Eltacolibre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2127_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T04:59:42-07:00","id":946870,"title":"","content":"There is currently a quite interesting thread over at rpg.net where someone is doing a &quot;[Let's Read/Compare] Exalted 1e, 2e &amp; 3e core&quot; thread. It might be worth checking out.<br /> <br /> Personally, I prefer 2.x over the other editions, and while I think 3E might be a more technically solid system, neither the mechanics nor the setting changes are to my liking (but hey, there are quite a few things I'm throwing out from 2ed as well). However, there are things I really like about 3E; the new social interaction system for example. I might also go with the new map.<br /> <br /> So, in my opinion, it really comes down to gaming style and preferences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T05:01:18-07:00","id":946872,"title":"","content":"While the Infernal may have been gutted with the errata, I have to say, at least there are Charms to gut, you know? Plus, as much as I like the new system, people keep saying how much better it is because of so much playtesting. I agree that the system is cool, but, like, Stealth is already being reworked...so...if that's our gauge...<br /> <br /> Anyway, both myself and many others have made 2E work just fine. I remember when it came out and everyone was so excited that the rules were better than 1st edition and I kind of feel 3E is doing the same. Whatever. Like what you like, but to claim it's a game that's not playable when I damn well know it is just to promote the newest edition...well...it smacks of fanboy, that's all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1101-blindst","name":"blindST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T05:20:40-07:00","id":946878,"title":"","content":"Out of curiosity, what do you mean about stealth being reworked?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9749-andrew-d","name":"Andrew D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T05:42:32-07:00","id":946890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=946860#post946860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People do play FATAL. Doesn't mean it's playable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes it does.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blindST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=946833#post946833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you should go with 2E. The way it sounds, I think the abundance of material for 2nd edition is something you'll really like. And it's AMAZINGLY well written. Both the Abyssal and Infernal books are just a delight to read.</div> </div> </div> </div>I cannot disagree forcefully enough. My experience is so absolutely opposite yours that I honestly thought you were joking at first.<br /> <br /> I have heard the Abyssal book called many things, but never a delight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blindST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=946872#post946872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whatever. Like what you like, but to claim it's a game that's not playable when I damn well know it is just to promote the newest edition...well...it smacks of fanboy, that's all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Claiming the side that disagrees with you are just fanboys has never been a constructive way to argue.<br /> <br /> 2e had bottom-level mechanical issues that impeded play as well as numerous unchecked writing trends that led to an unflattering distortion of concepts introduced in first edition. After years of playing it all of my games were held together with cobwebs, hope, mutually assured destruction and reams of houserules. If you had fun with it, that's great, so did I, but there's no pretending that it was not very deeply flawed on multiple levels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 08-09-2016, 10:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-09T19:03:02-07:00","id":947400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=946890#post946890\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I cannot disagree forcefully enough. My experience is so absolutely opposite yours that I honestly thought you were joking at first.<br /> <br /> I have heard the Abyssal book called many things, but never a delight.<br /> <br /> Claiming the side that disagrees with you are just fanboys has never been a constructive way to argue.<br /> <br /> 2e had bottom-level mechanical issues that impeded play as well as numerous unchecked writing trends that led to an unflattering distortion of concepts introduced in first edition. After years of playing it all of my games were held together with cobwebs, hope, mutually assured destruction and reams of houserules. If you had fun with it, that's great, so did I, but there's no pretending that it was not very deeply flawed on multiple levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's go piece by piece: That's unfortunate. I ran 1st and 2nd Edition for many years and it was a lot of fun for everyone involved. I've heard the same reasoning for why people don't like whatever game, they had a bad experience, but, honestly, I think that has less to do with the game and more to do with the people involved. Even Rifts can be fun with the right people.<br /> <br /> The Abyssal book is a great read. The first two chapters are amazing. I've heard people have issues with it mechanically, but see my opinion on that above.<br /> <br /> I wasn't claiming the side that disagrees are fanboys, but I have noticed a devotion among specific posters that boarders on slavish. Also, this isn't an argument. This was me giving an opinion. If you want to argue, we can, but I don't see the point.<br /> <br /> Every game, literally every single one, has flaws. The idea that there's a game that isn't flawed is, in itself, flawed thinking. It's the same idea with balance. There is no balance in games but what we make. This is an illusion. I would like you to name one game that's flawless, but I promise you, I will find a flaw. <br /> <br /> I'm wondering, however, as you see this as an argument, do you not see the huge flaws in the newest edition? I mean, if all versions of the game are flawed, there is no right answer but what we think, thus, we are all working on opinion, so there can be no clear winner or loser, making an argument on the subject a waste of time at best.<br /> <br /> In the end, to everyone that says &quot;&lt;Blank Game&gt; sucks because of rules&quot; really means &quot;My GM/ST/DM couldn't cut it&quot;, but, hey, once again, just opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1101-blindst","name":"blindST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T00:47:54-07:00","id":947589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blindST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=947400#post947400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let's go piece by piece: That's unfortunate. I ran 1st and 2nd Edition for many years and it was a lot of fun for everyone involved. I've heard the same reasoning for why people don't like whatever game, they had a bad experience, but, honestly, I think that has less to do with the game and more to do with the people involved. Even Rifts can be fun with the right people.<br /> <br /> The Abyssal book is a great read. The first two chapters are amazing. I've heard people have issues with it mechanically, but see my opinion on that above.<br /> <br /> I wasn't claiming the side that disagrees are fanboys, but I have noticed a devotion among specific posters that boarders on slavish. Also, this isn't an argument. This was me giving an opinion. If you want to argue, we can, but I don't see the point.<br /> <br /> Every game, literally every single one, has flaws. The idea that there's a game that isn't flawed is, in itself, flawed thinking. It's the same idea with balance. There is no balance in games but what we make. This is an illusion. I would like you to name one game that's flawless, but I promise you, I will find a flaw. <br /> <br /> I'm wondering, however, as you see this as an argument, do you not see the huge flaws in the newest edition? I mean, if all versions of the game are flawed, there is no right answer but what we think, thus, we are all working on opinion, so there can be no clear winner or loser, making an argument on the subject a waste of time at best.<br /> <br /> In the end, to everyone that says &amp;quot;&lt;Blank Game&gt; sucks because of rules&amp;quot; really means &amp;quot;My GM/ST/DM couldn't cut it&amp;quot;, but, hey, once again, just opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that no ruleset is perfect doesn't mean that some aren't more flawed than others. <br /> <br /> Plus nice use of the Oberoni fallacy there at the end. Way to have an insulting opinion towards all the STs who saw their campaign crumble under bad rules in way they hadn't foreseen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T02:03:20-07:00","id":947613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LeTipex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=947589#post947589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus nice use of the Oberoni fallacy there at the end. Way to have an insulting opinion towards all the STs who saw their campaign crumble under bad rules in way they hadn't foreseen.</div> </div> </div> </div>But is it more insulting than all the trash talking of those that prefer that system? No system fits everyone, and more often than not it is a question of a bad fit, not of bad rules. By the logic quite a few have used, Ex3 is badly broken because it don't fit me.<br /> <br /> blindST could perhaps had expressed it in another way, but this place do have a high hostility toward 2ed. Personally, I'm baffled why so many have to validate their liking of Ex3 by trash talking 2ed. To my understanding, blindST prefer the Ex3 mechanics over 2ed, but just happens to like 2ed too.<br /> <br /> IMNSHO: Neither 2ed nor Ex3 are broken; they are different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T02:54:50-07:00","id":947632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=947613#post947613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But is it more insulting than all the trash talking of those that prefer that system? No system fits everyone, and more often than not it is a question of a bad fit, not of bad rules. By the logic quite a few have used, Ex3 is badly broken because it don't fit me.<br /> <br /> blindST could perhaps had expressed it in another way, but this place do have a high hostility toward 2ed. Personally, I'm baffled why so many have to validate their liking of Ex3 by trash talking 2ed. To my understanding, blindST prefer the Ex3 mechanics over 2ed, but just happens to like 2ed too.<br /> <br /> IMNSHO: Neither 2ed nor Ex3 are broken; they are different.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think I've ever seen someone here say that those who prefered 2ed where just bad STs who &quot;couldn't cut it&quot;, so yeah, a bit more insulting.<br /> <br /> And no, 2ed is not badly broken because it doesn't fit the playstyle of some. It's badly broken because you can, using RAW, mind control someone into killing their child by asking something unrelated ten times in a row, because combat is a perfect-or-die slogfest where you can have two dozen charms and combo and still loose to someone who only has a perfect defense, and where you can build a manse that mass-produces hundreds of trained Dragon-Blooded or sorcerers each month.<br /> <br /> Now, to be fair, I still enjoyed 2ed! I ST'd two whole campaigns under that edition, and we had fun! But we had fun because we were willing to overlook the cracks and purposefully avoid them. But really, it's not &quot;trash-talking&quot; 2ed than admitting that Ex3 is a better ruleset, even if it's sometimes flawed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T03:07:13-07:00","id":947639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blindST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=947400#post947400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's go piece by piece: That's unfortunate. I ran 1st and 2nd Edition for many years and it was a lot of fun for everyone involved. I've heard the same reasoning for why people don't like whatever game, they had a bad experience, but, honestly, I think that has less to do with the game and more to do with the people involved. Even Rifts can be fun with the right people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. I too ran both prior editions and enjoyed them. It required perseverance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blindST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=947400#post947400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Abyssal book is a great read. The first two chapters are amazing. I've heard people have issues with it mechanically, but see my opinion on that above.</div> </div> </div> </div>I found reading both the Abyssal and Infernal books an absolutely wretched experience that saddened and angered me, and not because of their mechanics. I think I'm in a minority with Infernals, but not Abyssals. Agree to disagree there, I guess.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blindST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=947400#post947400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't claiming the side that disagrees are fanboys, but I have noticed a devotion among specific posters that boarders on slavish. Also, this isn't an argument. This was me giving an opinion. If you want to argue, we can, but I don't see the point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Presenting your arguments as an opinion doesn't mean you're not arguing. We're disagreeing on something and talking over both sides. That's an argument! That's what that is. It's not a bad thing, and it's not necessarily aggressive, there's no need to be so evasive about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blindST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=947400#post947400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every game, literally every single one, has flaws. The idea that there's a game that isn't flawed is, in itself, flawed thinking. It's the same idea with balance. There is no balance in games but what we make. This is an illusion. I would like you to name one game that's flawless, but I promise you, I will find a flaw.<br /> <br /> I'm wondering, however, as you see this as an argument, do you not see the huge flaws in the newest edition? I mean, if all versions of the game are flawed, there is no right answer but what we think, thus, we are all working on opinion, so there can be no clear winner or loser, making an argument on the subject a waste of time at best.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. I was actually quite disappointed when it first came out, because my experience in playing was not too dissimilar to my last 2e game in terms of rules complexity, ease of use and other factors. Then I went to my last 2e game and realized the <i>labyrinth</i> of house rules and gentleman's agreements that were required to keep it afloat. Don't use this Charm, homebrew that martial arts style, free excellencies, chargen revision, revised system for mass combat, revised system for grappling, rewritten profiles for NPCs and on and on and on.<br /> <br /> 3e's issues are dwarfed in comparison. Maybe you used canon 2e grappling and mass combat and Sidereal Martial Arts and Honored Companion of the Sun without running into any issues, I don't know.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blindST</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=947400#post947400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the end, to everyone that says &quot;&lt;Blank Game&gt; sucks because of rules&quot; really means &quot;My GM/ST/DM couldn't cut it&quot;, but, hey, once again, just opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really, though? &quot;My GM/ST/DM couldn't cut it&quot; certainly puts some blame on the game. Try rephrasing it as &quot;This game would require too much revision work to bother with.&quot; After years of playing 2e it was still finding new ways to screw with me, so I can certainly see why people would feel that way. I persevered because I enjoyed the setting, not the game. 3e works right out of the box with a few entirely avoidable quirks. After playing it for just a few months I'm already having more fun with it than I ever had with 1e and 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 08-10-2016, 06:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T05:01:49-07:00","id":947675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LeTipex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=947632#post947632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And no, 2ed is not badly broken because it doesn't fit the playstyle of some. It's badly broken because you can, using RAW, mind control someone into killing their child by asking something unrelated ten times in a row, because combat is a perfect-or-die slogfest where you can have two dozen charms and combo and still loose to someone who only has a perfect defense, and where you can build a manse that mass-produces hundreds of trained Dragon-Blooded or sorcerers each month.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I wouldn't use the Crafting system in Ex3 even if I was paid for it. It really was a &quot;are they fucking kidding me&quot; moment as I looked through that. It might be well balanced, but for me, those rules are a close second to the mechanics of FATAL for me of things I won't use. So that the RAW social influence mechanics of 2ed barely register on my &quot;bad mechanics&quot; scale (but as I tend to mention, the social mechanic rules of Ex3 is one of the things I'm considering porting over).<br /> <br /> Still, some love how the the crafting is made in Ex3, and even more like Ex3 as a whole. So, obviously it isn't a bad system, just a bad match for me.<br /> <br /> Personally, I might continue to poke around with &quot;Edition L&quot;, which probably is 50% 2ed, 20% 1st ed, 20% Ex3, and 10% other (which I probably never will put in any comprehensive format, as I don't even bother with my own rules as written).<br /> <br /> The reason I don't bounce my thoughts and ideas in this forum is because of the discussion climate here. The reason I'm still here is because I do find interesting ideas, and Exalted isn't the only WW or OPP game I'm interested in, and I haven't found another site I feel I want to talk about Exalted on. To the look of it, I'm not the only one that want to talk more about Exalted, from a 2ed perspective, but don't want to do it in the discussion climate of this site.<br /> <br /> The crafting system isn't the only thing that I dislike with Ex3. But beside this post, I have not mentioned how bad that ill fit is, as I can do it in a more neutral manner without being antagonistic. I think it is very likely that Ex3 is doing what it attempt to do a lot better than what 2ed is at doing what it tries to do. But they are trying to do different things, just as Cortex Classic and Cortex+ is two very different systems.<br /> <br /> TL;DR; we obviously want very different things from the system, and very different opinion of what is broken. I think you would dislike me talking about how broken I think Ex3 is as much I dislike all the talk of how broken 2ed is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2839,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","user":"Lundgren","date":"08-10-2016, 10:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T05:33:40-07:00","id":947690,"title":"","content":"I would just chime in to say that, in my experience, people can have very, very different experiences with game mechanics. So, I would take with a grain of salt any claim like &quot;this system is phenomenal&quot; or &quot;this is unplayable&quot;. For example, a lot of people found the Fair Folk 1E book unplayable and impossible to understand -- with the exception of the Mountain Folk chapter, which they praised highly for clearness, cleverness, and coolness. I found the Mountain Folk chapter one of the dumbest, least original, and most broken pieces of work in 1E. But the rest of the Fair Folk book ... oh, what a work of genius: beautiful, clever, well-written, easy to understand, and incredibly fun to play. The best product produced by WW, ever!<br /> <br /> That said, my group and I found the 2E mechanics painful -- overly complicated, and not well balanced. So much that we never made the switch from 1E except for a handful of &quot;trial' sessions. With the possible exception of the massive re-write known as 2.5E (with which I have almost no familiarity), I would recommend 1E over 2E. <br /> <br /> As for 3E... Well, I have played three sessions of 3E so far, but I can say this. It's nice, I like it better than 2E. However.<br /> First, while you *can* play with just the corebook... I really miss the other books. From gods and demons, to other Exalted, to the Fair Folk... a handful of QCs only go so far (though I can happily live without any &quot;books of artifacts&quot; or location books -- for the latter, I'll just use Scavenger Sons, which I think beats handily any other location product of the Exalted line).<br /> Second, mechanically 3E is nice, but it's not perfect. It feels as if it is based on very sound design principles, with some rather shoddy work on top. It's not just the craft charmset. It's a lot of little things, the way charms are written in a slightly ambiguous fashion that makes people ask &quot;does &quot;until next action&quot; include next action&quot; or &quot;how are clashes and counterattacks dealt with&quot; etc. Then again, the fact that the principles are sound means that it's not too hard to rebuild the top layer to one's liking (in fact, some fans have already done great work in this direction, so you might find the work done for you).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12189-nessuno","name":"nessuno","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"26"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-10T06:51:12-07:00","id":947732,"title":"","content":"So, for the OP, I think you should just check both out and see what you like. We all seem to have different opinions for a lot of different reasons. As they say, your mileage may vary. I, again, personally think it comes down to: Superior System with lack of Support or Mediocre System with tons of Support. Make up your own mind. We've all been too clouded by personal bias to give you a better run down than that I think. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1101-blindst","name":"blindST","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1101_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T05:16:53-07:00","id":953758,"title":"","content":"Just a curiosity as someone that has been playing Ex2.5 for a bit under 3 years (and loving it) but has no experience about any other iteration of the system (I read 1st edition but didn't like it much at the time, but honestly it's been too long ago to even remember why... and went back to 2e by chance later when I switched workplace and joined some colleagues. Still haven't read or tried 3rd) <br /> What exactly is so broken/imbalanced in it? <br /> Because I never found anything like that yet, and I did my best! At worst I found stuff that wasn't as cool as I wished :P <br /> <br /> As far as the complexity of the system itself, I sort of like complicated systems but I admit that rules are a bit to spread out around and not well organized (I mean, there's charms for solars hidden inside the alchemical book without even a sidebar or index entry about it). Plus there's some holes I'd have loved to see it filled with a bit more than &quot;lol, just do whatever and see if the storyteller runs with it&quot;, like artifact crafting (while manse crafting is quite better).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7835-bard","name":"Bard","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T10:23:52-07:00","id":953900,"title":"","content":"Honestly, if you and your group haven't found the things that are broken and imbalanced in it... I kind of don't want to tell you.<br /> <br /> If the players don't realise and don't utilise it in a broken way, the game's quite fun. But once they understand how to break it... ugh. Combats are so, so, so dull. And then you die horribly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T11:02:25-07:00","id":953917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=953758#post953758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What exactly is so broken/imbalanced in it?<br /> Because I never found anything like that yet, and I did my best! At worst I found stuff that wasn't as cool as I wished :P</div> </div> </div> </div>2nd edition wasn't exactly broken (though there were a lot of broken widgets like certain Charms or Charmsets), rather it's just that it kind of stops being fun once all the players have an array perfect defenses (not hard to get) and they can't really be threatened anymore other than spending several hours slowly running down their mote pool.<br /> <br /> If your group has a &quot;gentleman's agreement&quot; where the ST doesn't throw people capable of one-shotting the PCs (like Earth Immaculates wielding grand goremauls), and the PC's don't rely on attacks that will one-shot the Storyteller's NPCs, so that combat doesn't just come down to the players and their enemies throwing one-shot killing attacks at one another and responding with perfect defenses another until one side runs out of Essence and dies, then there's really nothing wrong with 2nd edition.<br /> <br /> It's just that the base game was designed around high-lethality attacks capable of one-shotting people, countered by inexpensive, spammable perfect defenses and when you get down to it, that's not really a whole lot of fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T11:52:10-07:00","id":953935,"title":"","content":"I guess growing up where Drakar och Demoner (a RQ/BRP derivate) was the norm, where the risk of one-shot deaths existed in any combat (and nothing was ever &quot;balanced&quot;), instead of D&amp;D, might be part of why I don't have a problem with 2.x.<br /> <br /> I also have a hard to seeing how a ST regularly throwing goremaul wielding opponents on the PC's being the fault of the system.<br /> <br /> Sounds more like cultural clash, and non-matching expectations, than broken <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T12:05:55-07:00","id":953940,"title":"","content":"Another way 2.x is supposed to be broken, that I have seen mentioned quite a few times, is in how it is impossible to make a &quot;challenging encounter&quot; for the Dawn, without more or less instantly wiping out the rest of the circle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T12:07:22-07:00","id":953943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=953935#post953935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also have a hard to seeing how a ST regularly throwing goremaul wielding opponents on the PC's being the fault of the system.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is what that leads to when you also have cheap, spammable, perfect defenses.<br /> <br /> ST: The Lunar attacks you with his grand goremaul which can kill you in one hit.<br /> <br /> PC: I perfectly defend for 3 motes, because if I don't, I'm dead. This leaves me with 57 motes of Essence.<br /> <br /> ST: Okay. Your turn.<br /> <br /> Player: I make an attack against the Lunar with my grand grimscythe which can kill him in one hit.<br /> <br /> ST: He perfectly defends for 4 motes because if he doesn't, he's dead. Your Essence Sight tells you he has 63 motes remaining. His turn now. He attacks you with his grand goremaul which can kill you in one hit.<br /> <br /> PC: I perfectly defend for 3 motes because if I don't, I'm dead. This leaves me with 54 motes of Essence.<br /> <br /> ST: Okay. Your turn.<br /> <br /> Player: I make an attack against the Lunar with my grand grimscythe which can kill him in one hit.. Since he used Charm X which has Y weakness, I will attack him in a way to take advantage of Y and bypass his perfect defense.<br /> <br /> ST: He perfectly defends by using Z Charm which doesn't have that weakness for 4 motes, because if he doesn't, he'd be dead. Your Essence Sight tells you he has 59 motes remaining. His turn now. He attacks you with his grand goremaul which can kill you in one hit.<br /> <br /> Well, you get the point.<br /> <br /> This is what combat turns into - a slow slog to see which person can bleed the other out of Essence first. Sure players and the ST can try to stunt and spice things up for the attack (which is meaningless since the attack will just be perfectly parried), but at the core, this is what high lethality coupled with cheap spammable attacks leads to.<br /> <br /> Basically it's just kind of boring for everybody involved. If your group managed to avoid that happening, cool. But a lot of people ran into this problem, which was a core facet of the Exalted game engine, and one of the big reasons why they decided to alter it in the new edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T15:32:52-07:00","id":954064,"title":"","content":"in Ex2.5 Perfect defs aren't cheap anymore, they start at 8 motes for a single attack iirc (so against even a mundane 2 attacks flurry is 16... parring for a WHOLE tick starts using willpower), and if you want to have motes to do an attack big enough to pass scene-long and passive defenses you can't do too many perfects. Still, we did notice the issue with that (as in, if you are completely focused into anything that is not combat, you're dead meat at the first hit), but since the start we saw it as a part of the game... huge attacks that if they hit they kill if you don't defend, and it goes both ways... we always rolled with it and planned accordingly, being all mighty and godlike on the common rabble and careful with the exalted. My character has almost no soak and no parry and still alive. The 2.5 Defend Other action is quite useful <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> The real issue I find is a high number of attacks from flurries or multiple attackers really, as the minimum damage, even if it's just 1 now, stacks fast, especially considering how rare healing is in 2e. (Solars and Lunar have regen, but only Dragon Kings iirc can heal)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7835,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7835-bard","user":"Bard","date":". 08-19-2016, 06:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7835-bard","name":"Bard","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T15:54:56-07:00","id":954077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=953935#post953935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also have a hard to seeing how a ST regularly throwing goremaul wielding opponents on the PC's being the fault of the system.</div> </div> </div> </div>A DB with a goremaul is only one example, is the thing. There are <i>lots</i> of things that can be instantly fatal in 2e: Poison. Surprise attacks. Five mortals with sledges. Heck, DB anima flux can do it in pretty short order.<br /> <br /> ... Right up until everyone has a standard suite of Nothing Can Kill Me Charms, and then the game becomes slow, predictable, and boring.<br /> <br /> That's all fine if you're playing a game where sudden meaningless death is the norm, but that's not exactly what Exalted promised. Most people didn't buy 2e and study its literal hundreds of combat Charms with the assumption that there were no actual combat decisions to make.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T18:07:47-07:00","id":954133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=954077#post954077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's all fine if you're playing a game where sudden meaningless death is the norm, but that's not exactly what Exalted promised. Most people didn't buy 2e and study its literal hundreds of combat Charms with the assumption that there were no actual combat decisions to make.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or a game where fighting to the death isn't a focus.<br /> <br /> I got into Exalted after the 2.5 errata was released, so I don't know how first or second edition was originally sold/promised. My interpretation is that Exalted promise the option of a lot of trivial fighting, but actual challenging fights are rare, dangerous, and preferable avoidable. From that perspective, when a fight then isn't avoidable, and it isn't a duel to the first blood or an option to yield, then it probably isn't a meaningless death, even if it is sudden.<br /> <br /> Poisons have to be delivered, surprise attacks have to be set up and can fail, the five mortals probably aren't teleported right next to the Exalted. So from my point of view, there are options to detect and handle the situation.<br /> <br /> So I guess 2.x supports more than one gaming style. <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> However, gaming where there are quite a few challenging combat encounters, where system mastery and tactical gaming are a focus, probably isn't one of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T19:27:44-07:00","id":954150,"title":"","content":"2.5 made perfect defenses significantly harder to use... but did it address lethality? The one time I played a game with pregen chars, the Dawn PC and Abyssal end-boss killed each other in one combat round, partly due to flurries and refusing to defend.<br /> <br /> When people talk about the high lethality, it leads me to wonder how many defense Charms a PC needs to start with just to not die as soon as combat starts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T19:28:04-07:00","id":954151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=954133#post954133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or a game where fighting to the death isn't a focus.<br /> <br /> I got into Exalted after the 2.5 errata was released, so I don't know how first or second edition was originally sold/promised. My interpretation is that Exalted promise the option of a lot of trivial fighting, but actual challenging fights are rare, dangerous, and preferable avoidable. From that perspective, when a fight then isn't avoidable, and it isn't a duel to the first blood or an option to yield, then it probably isn't a meaningless death, even if it is sudden.<br /> <br /> Poisons have to be delivered, surprise attacks have to be set up and can fail, the five mortals probably aren't teleported right next to the Exalted. So from my point of view, there are options to detect and handle the situation.<br /> <br /> So I guess 2.x supports more than one gaming style. <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> However, gaming where there are quite a few challenging combat encounters, where system mastery and tactical gaming are a focus, probably isn't one of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>2.x revised things for the better in a lot of ways. But look: the point I'm trying to make is that pre-2.5 2e was a <i>minefield</i>, that things you <i>thought</i> were going to be trivial fights wound up being murderous.<br /> <br /> Five guys with sledges is, to judge from the fiction, a trivial fight for an Exalt. Except, oops, the fifth guy gets an auto-surprise attack, hits your DV 0 for <i>stupid</i> damage, and now you're dead.<br /> <br /> Or maybe you just had one attacker throwing an ambush, to be at all clever and different - a sneaky rogue type, who poisoned his knives. Which hit, because DV 0 vs. surprise attacks - and a PC is dead.<br /> <br /> Okay, so no poison, just a couple of ninjas throwing daggers - whoops, still dead.<br /> <br /> Okay, so no stealth, just a couple of guys - but less than five! And they're a team, so they'll coordinate attacks. Except, shoot, the Zenith didn't bother to buy a penalty negator, figuring he could rely on his Excellency. Which he could, right up until he took eight attacks with a -4 coordination penalty, and now he's dead.<br /> <br /> Okay, no more people! T-rexes. We're going to fight t-rexes for a while - heck, that was even the meme for a bit, wasn't it? So we throw in a tyrant lizard, and the players annihilate it. Next time, we try two big similar monsters - except, <i>shoot</i>, that's all it takes for one of them to get a surprise attack when they're that big. That... doesn't make any sense, but that's what the book says - aaaaaand, yep, dead.<br /> <br /> We haven't even added anything that can spend Essence yet! We haven't thrown in a Dragon-Blood, who can kill you <i>by standing near you</i>, or a low-Essence god who <i>happens</i> to have Essence Bite and Principle of Motion, or <i>heaven forbid</i> a Sidereal with any SMA at all out of Scroll of the Monk. We've just been fighting mortals. We shouldn't need to be worried yet.<br /> <br /> And yet we keep dying.<br /> <br /> And then the players get <i>smart</i>. They get Reflex Sidestep Technique. They get Seven Shadows Evasion. They get Dipping Swallow Defense, and Fivefold Bulwark Stance, and Leaping Dodge Method, and Iron Skin Concentration, and Infinite (Whatever) Mastery, and they run a really solid &quot;rely on your DV, soak it if that fails,&quot; build. And they fight as close to mote-neutral as it's possible to get, with their decision plan sufficiently automated that you comfortably summarize it on a post-it note -<br /> <br /> - and that's every fight for the rest of the game.<br /> <br /> You talk about fights to first blood and yielding and so on, but when I pick up the book, I read about Wyld Hunts that want to kill me and normal people that think Solars are demons, and then I get fights that allow trivial mortals to murder my glorious god-king unless I take a <i>precise</i> combination of Charms. Not everyone who played 2e played in a style that ran into this problem, but <i>lots</i> of people did. This isn't just a &quot;People were running the game with the wrong style&quot; thing - if you ran 2.0 out of the box, as it described itself, with no prior instruction, you had a high probability of a no-warning failure state.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 08-19-2016, 10:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-19T19:38:04-07:00","id":954154,"title":"","content":"Exalted having fights that are brutal, short and best avoided is itself a failure state for the game, even if people do find that playstyle enjoyable. It'd be fine to have a system that promotes that approach to combat if you were trying to play old school D&amp;D or Shadowrun or something, but Exalted was never supposed to do that. High-budget anime fights are and always were supposed to be a big part of the game, and any edition that fails to support that has failed at being Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T04:51:35-07:00","id":954306,"title":"","content":"How much of reduced lethality in 3e is due to superior explanation (the book tells you what you need better) and lowballed opponents? 3e has a lot of customization, so it seems like it would be possible to built a lot of bad builds that crumple. Or isn't that an issue in practice (because the customization isn't much in the baseline survival things)?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=954154#post954154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exalted having fights that are brutal, short and best avoided is itself a failure state for the game, even if people do find that playstyle enjoyable. It'd be fine to have a system that promotes that approach to combat if you were trying to play old school D&amp;D or Shadowrun or something, but Exalted was never supposed to do that. High-budget anime fights are and always were supposed to be a big part of the game, and any edition that fails to support that has failed at being Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ideally, I'd think Storytellers and players could sort of collaborate to make fights work to their expectation, of how short or long they want it to be. Players build characters who win or lose in relatively few moves, STs build opponents who do likewise. How many moves do really good, well choreographed fight scenes in great action anime and live action really have? Sometimes very few.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=953943#post953943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is what combat turns into - a slow slog to see which person can bleed the other out of Essence first. Sure players and the ST can try to stunt and spice things up for the attack (which is meaningless since the attack will just be perfectly parried), but at the core, this is what high lethality coupled with cheap spammable attacks leads to.<br /> <br /> Basically it's just kind of boring for everybody involved. If your group managed to avoid that happening, cool. But a lot of people ran into this problem, which was a core facet of the Exalted game engine, and one of the big reasons why they decided to alter it in the new edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though I guess it's not so much the Essence drain bit itself that seems bad about all that you describe, but that there are no real options and gambling and guessing. <br /> <br /> The way you describe it there isn't the play options of &quot;Well, if I do X, but he reacts that way, then on the next move I would be able to do Y, which would ultimately put me in the essence advantage... but if he reacts another way, I wouldn't be, so I'll do this that'll push him to react that way&quot;. It's all very predetermined.<br /> <br /> Seems like you could probably build all that into a framework of perfects and essence, with tactical advantage states and status effects, and get something that works out as a good game. Perhaps one as fun as 3e. It's not, y'know, impossible. But IIUC, 2.5 wasn't there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T05:53:46-07:00","id":954325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=954151#post954151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't just a &quot;People were running the game with the wrong style&quot; thing - if you ran 2.0 out of the box, as it described itself, with no prior instruction, you had a high probability of a no-warning failure state.</div> </div> </div> </div>In part, it is a matter of ones attitude to a rule system to begin with; Rules as Written vs. Rules as Intended vs. Rules as Suggestions. In part, what the expectations of the setting are, and ones willingness to approximate or tweak them. Then it also is a matter of what kind of focus the group wants (political intrigue or culture gaming, for example, will by its own nature not be as affected by the combat system). A lot of different factors will affect if a system is a good fit, and it can even be a good or a bad fit for a particular group, depending on whom in the group will be the ST.<br /> <br /> It is very possible that the descriptions in 2.0 promoted a gaming style it sucked at, but as I came in late and have the attitude that I have to what is written, I don't really have an opinion in that regard.<br /> <br /> Hopefully, EX3 will continue to be a better fit for a lot of people. Even if Ex3 is a poor fit for me (not saying 2ed is a perfect fit for me, just a better one), and I will mainly use it for mining for ideas, I'm glad they took it in a new direction. We who prefer first or second edition can easily get our hands on the old books through Ebay or DriveThruStuff. So it isn't like the existence of one removes the others.<br /> <br /> EX3 will be a poor fit for some, even if it happens to be a minority, and for them one of the other editions might fit better. As there are some setting changes between the editions, one might be a better choice over another even if they plan to use Wushu/BESM/UniSystem/DC Heroes/God Bound/Whatever for the mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T07:33:26-07:00","id":954371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=954325#post954325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In part, it is a matter of ones attitude to a rule system to begin with; Rules as Written vs. Rules as Intended vs. Rules as Suggestions. In part, what the expectations of the setting are, and ones willingness to approximate or tweak them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's fine as far as it goes, but when people are critiquing 2e, they're necessarily critiquing 2e as written and not some hypothetical game that's kinda like 2e, except with all the fatal and boring parts fixed. And 2e <i>as written</i> is pretty bad; people could and did houserule or table-contract around that, but the actual written game was bad.<br /> <br /> If one never used the combat rules, or, heck, never used <i>any</i> of the rules, then sure, they wouldn't cause problems - but that's not really a defense.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=954306#post954306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much of reduced lethality in 3e is due to superior explanation (the book tells you what you need better) and lowballed opponents? 3e has a lot of customization, so it seems like it would be possible to built a lot of bad builds that crumple. Or isn't that an issue in practice (because the customization isn't much in the baseline survival things)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think the explanation is a <i>big</i> part of it, though it's probably some. Some of the big factors driving 3e's reduced lethality that I see: weapon stats scale better (i.e., they scale up less, and they outstrip armor less); many really nasty effects (damage, poison) require Decisives, which are harder to land and generally need several rounds of build-up first; many auto-death states (surprise attacks, the fifth man &quot;free strike&quot; rule, Coordination penalties) have either been scaled back or eliminated...<br /> <br /> ... and, yeah, the fact that all anyone has to fight right now are relatively-dinky QCs. Who, notably, <i>tend </i>not to have terrifying first-strike capability, with the exception of Ahlat (who is entirely capable of murdering you through several Ox-Bodies as the first action of combat, if you don't have a perfect defense handy).<br /> <br /> Solar-on-Solar fights, from my tests, still have lots of potential to end in one-round chunky salsa. Solar Melee has the OWTB/PBA/IWA/PBA/IWA/etc. combo. Brawl has Heaven Thunder Hammer, for ~10L falling damage that can be triggered <i>after</i> hitting you. Thrown + Stealth + Larceny gets you that &quot;Open the fight in Stealth, lead with two 30i+ Decisives&quot; combo. Any of those have a good chance of being one-round fatal - so I suspect Exalt fights are still going to be pretty enormously deadly. But <i>mortals</i> have been scaled back a ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T08:09:10-07:00","id":954385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=954371#post954371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's fine as far as it goes, but when people are critiquing 2e, they're necessarily critiquing 2e as written and not some hypothetical game that's kinda like 2e, except with all the fatal and boring parts fixed. And 2e <i>as written</i> is pretty bad; people could and did houserule or table-contract around that, but the actual written game was bad.<br /> <br /> If one never used the combat rules, or, heck, never used <i>any</i> of the rules, then sure, they wouldn't cause problems - but that's not really a defense.</div> </div> </div> </div>And people are already talking about broken builds in EX3, and I can see a lot of houserules rewrites. Odds are, someone might figure out a &quot;single strategy&quot; there as well. Personally, I take 2.0 RAW over EX3 RAW if I had to pick one of them, and not being allowed to houserule. That's my preference.<br /> <br /> The StoryTeller has always been hard to foresee all the ways things might interact, and it has also been good at attracting those being turned off by systems created by &quot;engineers&quot;. Some StoryTeller variants are less stable than others, and I'm sure 2ed is less stable than EX3, as written. During my 30 years of gaming, I think there have only been two games I can play RAW (Star Wars D6 and James Bond), and SW D6 has a part I would have to houserule if I ever would bring that part into the game (how the dark side of the force is handled).<br /> <br /> So it comes back to me disagreeing on it being broken, and what it means with a system being broken. I think it is a good thing when people are warning those interested about potential potholes, preferable with a mention of ways to work around it. That gives the person the option to pick what suites them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T08:25:29-07:00","id":954396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=954385#post954385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And people are already talking about broken builds in EX3, and I can see a lot of houserules rewrites. Odds are, someone might figure out a &quot;single strategy&quot; there as well. Personally, I take 2.0 RAW over EX3 RAW if I had to pick one of them, and not being allowed to houserule. That's my preference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you played 2e RAW, or just 2.5? Because I'm saying this as one of the folks who has done the most rewriting of 3e, and has been a fairly outspoken critic of it: 3e might have broken builds, but 2e <i>was a deathtrap</i>. 3e might have broken Charms, but 2e was broken from the ground up.<br /> <br /> I suspect you're running with a fairly nonstandard definition of &quot;broken,&quot; here; it might help if you gave a clear definition of what that means, for you?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T08:41:45-07:00","id":954412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=954077#post954077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A DB with a goremaul is only one example, is the thing. There are <i>lots</i> of things that can be instantly fatal in 2e: Poison. Surprise attacks. Five mortals with sledges. Heck, DB anima flux can do it in pretty short order.<br /> <br /> ... Right up until everyone has a standard suite of Nothing Can Kill Me Charms, and then the game becomes slow, predictable, and boring.<br /> <br /> That's all fine if you're playing a game where sudden meaningless death is the norm, but that's not exactly what Exalted promised. Most people didn't buy 2e and study its literal hundreds of combat Charms with the assumption that there were no actual combat decisions to make.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, characters in Exalted 2E were just incredibly fragile. It was one of the first things that struck me, and I actually went to my ST asking if I was understanding something wrong.<br /> <br /> A normal Exalt has 7HP. A normal attack with basically no enhancers nor super amazing weapons (just basic artifact weapons) nor anything special, just plain &quot;I hit the dude&quot;, in a fight between Essence users can easily be around 15 damage dice. Substract a little from Soak, and you're left with a system where, <i>without any resources being spent</i>, people die in two hits in all probability. Especially because getting hit once reduces your ability to defend to such a segree that you are not going to dodge the following attack.<br /> <br /> Now add the myriad things Exalted allows for offense. Post-soak damage adders. Poison. Ambush. Shaping. Directed environmental effects. Excellencies. Grand artifact weapons, all of which hit for ridiculous damage and ignored half of soak. Damage doublers. The list goes on and on. Anything, if it spends any kind of juice, can kill you in a single hit. So people grow paranoid and abuse perfect defenses. And the rest is history.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T09:14:55-07:00","id":954431,"title":"","content":"2e is the superior game for a group that's not used to Exalted and hasn't put a lot of time into learning the rules. While certainly many methods exist to 'break' the game, they aren't discovered early on by a group that isn't interested in poking around for that sort of flaw.<br /> <br /> It adapts better to a new group because you don't need to understand the system to understand what you are buying, to such a degree. 3e has a complicated initiative system which is difficult to explain and even more difficult to fully anticipate in terms of mechanical interactions. In 3e, players who are totally new to the game and have no idea what they are doing will have a hard time choosing charms because they can't really understand the value of those charms.<br /> <br /> In 2e, even though the system may be less 'tight', charms are more or less far less complicated and easy to understand. They interact with a system that the ST needs to understand but the player doesn't. They can be explained in 'plain' terms once the basic system is understood. The utility of most of the charms in the 2e system is fairly obvious and straightforward with a few notable examples.<br /> <br /> Thus, the ST will spend far less time trying to clarify the value of abilities in 2e and also far less time trying to clarify the value of available-to-be-purchased abilities. Though the game will eventually break if players are interested in breaking it, 2e holds together reasonably well to a casual group and can run for years without issues.<br /> <br /> Therefore, I would without hesitation recommend 2e above 3e when starting from scratch with new players.<br /> <br /> 3e is a system for when people really get into 2e, stress test the fuck out of it, and then want a mechanically robust alternative. Those kind of players are willing to invest the time and energy into understanding the complicated mechanics themselves, so they can fully enjoy the 3e product and not feel confused or frustrated by it.<br /> <br /> Note, also, those are the people who post most often on the forums, so you may see a bit of selection bias in these replies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T09:55:43-07:00","id":954455,"title":"","content":"It was quite a while before we discovered how lethal 2E could be. Once we found out, the ingame changes were really interesting to me. Combat became a last resort option even amongst most essence using NPCs (lethality swung both ways). We also weren't thrilled with how long it took to resolve combat. We've been hoping for faster combat since 1E. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Back to ingame consequences, PCs and NPCs used other tactics against foes. Disruption of resources, social combat, trade/information wars, the occasional assassination against those not likely to have a reflexive paranoia combo, etc. Exalted who surrendered instead of fighting to the death were treated with respect like captured nobility or military officers and were ransomed.<br /> <br /> Of course that wasn't an option for the Solars when facing a Wyld Hunt. That's what made Wyld Hunts so dangerous; there was no negotiation. When the Solars did win, they stripped the Hunt of whatever Artifacts and Resources they had and turned surviving DBs loose with naught but a blanket. Additionally some Deathlords would convert captured Solars into Abyssals instead of ransoming them for other gains. So, it wasn't like not fighting to the death was always an option.<br /> <br /> So yeah, combat in 2E was really dangerous. Just like in real life! :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T09:56:37-07:00","id":954457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=954371#post954371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Solar-on-Solar fights, from my tests, still have lots of potential to end in one-round chunky salsa. Solar Melee has the OWTB/PBA/IWA/PBA/IWA/etc. combo. Brawl has Heaven Thunder Hammer, for ~10L falling damage that can be triggered <i>after</i> hitting you. Thrown + Stealth + Larceny gets you that &quot;Open the fight in Stealth, lead with two 30i+ Decisives&quot; combo. Any of those have a good chance of being one-round fatal - so I suspect Exalt fights are still going to be pretty enormously deadly. But <i>mortals</i> have been scaled back a ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. With Exalted 2E, it's starting from this basis of having a lot of &quot;free&quot; / non-Charm methods to be extremely lethal, many of which which mortals can use (some they can't like high artefact weapon damage) and even benefit more from (multiple attackers). Then Exalted were expected to buy lots of defenses straight out to offset (though without actually any practical basis in the system to encourage them to do, like gating offense behind basic defense) and build up from there. That's all due to the baseline inspiration of &quot;Ultra lethal, brutal, unpredictable low fantasy game for mortals, then Exalted use Charms to ignore this in favor of acting like wuxia-anime type heroes&quot;. <br /> <br /> But that combination of high base lethality and absolute defenses which cost the same if you hit them for high damage or low, meant increasing offense Charms often ended up redundant with the copious &quot;free&quot; lethality, (attacks need to just have X lethality threshold strong enough to force opponents to use their single cost defense, which artefact weapons already cover, and there's no advantage to enhancing an attack further). So everyone just spends on defense. When they understand the system, after a few (or quite a few) possible missteps.<br /> <br /> Ex3 then (among other things) solves by paring back and toning down the &quot;free&quot; lethality (including taming the potential of large squads of mortals to gang up on PCs, via implementing battlegroups), and if mortals stay are about as defensively squishy as they were, you would expect they would end up less of a threat (to one another and Exalts). Kind of funny when mortals being *more* effective in battle against Exalted was supposed to be one of the things Ex3 was going to have as a feature. At the same time, sounds like Ex3 has lots of lethality that can be built for by PCs who are really invested in it, or enemies who are built to be seriously lethal...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T13:26:45-07:00","id":954581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=954396#post954396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you played 2e RAW, or just 2.5? Because I'm saying this as one of the folks who has done the most rewriting of 3e, and has been a fairly outspoken critic of it: 3e might have broken builds, but 2e <i>was a deathtrap</i>. 3e might have broken Charms, but 2e was broken from the ground up.<br /> <br /> I suspect you're running with a fairly nonstandard definition of &quot;broken,&quot; here; it might help if you gave a clear definition of what that means, for you?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, I haven't played 2e RAW. As playing RAW is a gaming style I'm not interested in, even if I had I would never have played it long enough to run into the problem some people had with it. Now it sounds like we are heading into the Strict Kriegsspiel vs. Free Kriegsspiel argument, which goes back to the 19th century, and I feel like I'm going on like a broken record (hm... is that phrase making any sense to people who grew up with CD or mp3 players?) on everything else.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2839-lundgren","name":"Lundgren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T14:59:08-07:00","id":954633,"title":"","content":"Let me give you guys some background. My favorite tabletop is Dark Heresy. It is a game notorious for TPKs, lethal combat, and enemies that can wipe the PCs against the floor in a few turns. I still found 2e to be way too lethal. Worse, it was binary. There were no real gradients of power. At the end of the day, there was &quot;combat optimized Solar&quot; and &quot;about to be dead.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T19:19:14-07:00","id":954747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lundgren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=954581#post954581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope, I haven't played 2e RAW. As playing RAW is a gaming style I'm not interested in, even if I had I would never have played it long enough to run into the problem some people had with it. Now it sounds like we are heading into the Strict Kriegsspiel vs. Free Kriegsspiel argument, which goes back to the 19th century, and I feel like I'm going on like a broken record (hm... is that phrase making any sense to people who grew up with CD or mp3 players?) on everything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, I'm over 30; I understand the Strict/Free Kriegsspiel debate, even if I wasn't around for the D&amp;D 1e incarnation of those arguments. But, again, when people criticize 2e, they're criticizing <i>the game that was written</i>, and not the hodgepodge of &quot;rulings not rules&quot; that exists in any particular GM's head. I have no way of determining whether 2e As A Hypothetical GM Might Mentally Rewrite It is a better game than 3e AAHGMMRI is, but the 2e rules I actually <i>read</i> were bad.<br /> <br /> (I <i>also</i> think that 2e had some of the most brilliant and beautiful system-and-setting marriages I've ever seen - which 3e pointedly and deliberately does <i>not</i>. Nephilpal's work on Infernals and Glories is a master class in rules that are also stories. But those marriages were built on a foundation of boring, unfun, and spontaneously lethal combat. These are problems that 3e does not inherently have, and the problems 3e does have - its poor keywording, ambigous resolutions, and unclear verbiage, for instance - are not hard-coded into the game in the same way that lethality was.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":1376,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","user":"Irked","date":". 08-20-2016, 10:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T20:11:38-07:00","id":954767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=954412#post954412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, characters in Exalted 2E were just incredibly fragile. It was one of the first things that struck me, and I actually went to my ST asking if I was understanding something wrong.<br /> <br /> A normal Exalt has 7HP. A normal attack with basically no enhancers nor super amazing weapons (just basic artifact weapons) nor anything special, just plain &quot;I hit the dude&quot;, in a fight between Essence users can easily be around 15 damage dice. Substract a little from Soak, and you're left with a system where, <i>without any resources being spent</i>, people die in two hits in all probability. Especially because getting hit once reduces your ability to defend to such a segree that you are not going to dodge the following attack.<br /> <br /> Now add the myriad things Exalted allows for offense. Post-soak damage adders. Poison. Ambush. Shaping. Directed environmental effects. Excellencies. Grand artifact weapons, all of which hit for ridiculous damage and ignored half of soak. Damage doublers. The list goes on and on. Anything, if it spends any kind of juice, can kill you in a single hit. So people grow paranoid and abuse perfect defenses. And the rest is history.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just throwing this out there:<br /> <br /> the <u>average mortal</u> also has 7 health levels.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T20:14:36-07:00","id":954768,"title":"","content":"What's this about kriegsspiel?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T20:39:00-07:00","id":954777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=954768#post954768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's this about kriegsspiel?</div> </div> </div> </div>A wargame for training Prussian and German officers created in 1812. The original 'strict' rules were cumbersome and performing the calculations took more time and effort than the combat they were meant to simulate. So 'free' rules were devised to allow the game master more leniency in arbitrating the effect of players' commands.<br /> <br /> Basically, game players have been arguing over whether to use RAW or RAI for literally centuries. (Though not necessarily the <i>same </i>players.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T20:45:25-07:00","id":954781,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=954777#post954777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A wargame for training Prussian and German officers created in 1812. The original 'strict' rules were cumbersome and performing the calculations took more time and effort than the combat they were meant to simulate. So 'free' rules were devised to allow the game master more leniency in arbitrating the effect of players' commands.<br /> <br /> Basically, game players have been arguing over whether to use RAW or RAI for literally centuries. (Though not necessarily the <i>same </i>players.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. It's one of those &quot;Nobody's right or wrong, there are just different playstyles and preferences&quot; things.<br /> <br /> The trouble is that, while Free is a totally legit way to play (or, well, a totally legit end of the spectrum, since most people are somewhere between the two poles), there's no clear way to debate which game has superior Free rules, because part of playing Free is <i>disregarding the rules</i> when you don't like 'em. So, like, I have no idea whether 2e or 3e plays better under Free Kriegsspiel, because rules-wise, everyone who plays either game Free is playing a different game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-20T21:07:48-07:00","id":954793,"title":"","content":"3e also has a baked in death save, the choice to, once per story, take a crippling injury instead of dying. Which is nice, specially for STs that miscalculated something and don't want to be seen as being &quot;soft&quot; by players, for whatever reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T00:26:38-07:00","id":954871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=954793#post954793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3e also has a baked in death save, the choice to, once per story, take a crippling injury instead of dying. Which is nice, specially for STs that miscalculated something and don't want to be seen as being &quot;soft&quot; by players, for whatever reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also worth noting that checking off a character's incapacitated HL with lethal damage can simply mean that they are dying, not already dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10881-anasurimbor","name":"Anasurimbor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T02:13:32-07:00","id":954894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=954747#post954747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I <i>also</i> think that 2e had some of the most brilliant and beautiful system-and-setting marriages I've ever seen - which 3e pointedly and deliberately does <i>not</i>. Nephilpal's work on Infernals and Glories is a master class in rules that are also stories. But those marriages were built on a foundation of boring, unfun, and spontaneously lethal combat. These are problems that 3e does not inherently have, and the problems 3e does have - its poor keywording, ambigous resolutions, and unclear verbiage, for instance - are not hard-coded into the game in the same way that lethality was.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd agree with this. 3rd ed has some op charms, it has some vague writing, and so on, but the basic system is fine (except perhaps char gen, but let's not get into that). The basic system assumptions of 2nd ed were terrible.<br /> <br /> 2e was the game where I saw PCs kill other PCs entirely by accident more than any other game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T03:58:26-07:00","id":954902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anasurimbor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=954871#post954871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also worth noting that checking off a character's incapacitated HL with lethal damage can simply mean that they are dying, not already dead.</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bReally, given that premise, I have to question if it's necessary to ever kill a player character unless it's at a moment that everybody agrees is suitably dramatic or the player feels this is a good point to retire the character. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T07:41:25-07:00","id":954944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=954902#post954902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bReally, given that premise, I have to question if it's necessary to ever kill a player character unless it's at a moment that everybody agrees is suitably dramatic or the player feels this is a good point to retire the character.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't understand this line of thinking, and I don't think I ever will. Sorry, but no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T08:02:16-07:00","id":954950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=954944#post954944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't understand this line of thinking</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThere are issues with vagaries of chance throwing a whole game into tumult and possibly excluding one or more of the players early.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T08:32:00-07:00","id":954960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=954950#post954950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bThere are issues with vagaries of chance throwing a whole game into tumult and possibly excluding one or more of the players early.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not really, in my opinion.<br /> <br /> Many players forget that they will almost always have the option of &quot;fleeing&quot; from a lethal/possibly lethal situation. Running from combat, backing out of a bad social situation, etc, I almost always include some sort of &quot;out&quot;, but the PC's have to initiate it.<br /> <br /> In my games, you get <u>one</u> dice fudge, usually when the players are new or the campaign just started, but after that, that is it. The dice fall where they may. NOTE: I roll all the dice in my games, behind a screen. The Players handle the RP, while I get everything else.<br /> <br /> If a PC dies in my games, it is usually pretty much their fault. Either they did something stupid, got into combat with something that was way out of their league, or refused to pay attention to &quot;the way the wind was blowing&quot;. Get surrounded in combat? Your fault. Piss off the local authority figure? Your fault. Not recognize that the BBEG is probably gonna take you out if/when you cause a ruckus? Your fault.<br /> <br /> I don't treat my PC's any different than I do an NPC. They don't get any slack, either crunch or fluff wise. I find the whole idea preposterous, and vaguely patronizing, as a matter of fact.<br /> <br /> Asides, it takes about 5 minutes to make a new character. <br /> <br /> It also probably helps that I actually take the recently-deceased player aside and explain to them what they &quot;did wrong&quot; that led to character death. See if they understand the mechanics, or understood where a characters opinions and decisions were based.<br /> <br /> But, other than that, it is <u>my</u> story. The PCs are their characters to play, yes, but everything else is my decision. If the PC does something that would logically result in their death, then that is on them. I just run the world like it is &quot;supposed to&quot;. Don't want to get ambushed or assassinated? Don't mess with the wrong people, or hire counterspies/bodyguards. Don't want to get surrounded in combat and get ROFL-stomped? Don't fight as an individual, fight intelligently and bring backup. <br /> <br /> It is very simple. <u>Don't do stupid stuff</u>, and you will almost always survive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T08:55:35-07:00","id":954967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=954902#post954902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bReally, given that premise, I have to question if it's necessary to ever kill a player character unless it's at a moment that everybody agrees is suitably dramatic or the player feels this is a good point to retire the character.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is 100% how I run with PC death in my games.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Pronounced &quot;Monkey Pie&quot;<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/762726-actual-play-the-party-prelude-project\" target=\"_blank\">Find my actual play content here!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/656-monkipi","name":"Monkipi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar656_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"318"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T09:28:27-07:00","id":954984,"title":"","content":"Pah. That's for soft players. What kind of drama or sense of the risk does the game have then? No, if the players screw up, the dice roll as they do, maybe the players die.<br /> <br /> (On an unrelated note, I've yet to see a single PC die in 3rd ed, and I've run like 30 games of it so far. I haven't even seen anyone use their &quot;I lose an arm instead of dying&quot; ability that all PCs get. Though they do flee and hide more than they used to, because now they can tell when they're in trouble, when they're crashed or whatever. I suspect that War Lion Stance is a big reason for the lack of PC death. Anyway, the Devs certainly have fixed lethality!)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T09:33:06-07:00","id":954986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=954984#post954984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What kind of drama or sense of the risk does the game have then?</div> </div> </div> </div> What happens while you're incapacitated, what the active characters need to do to revive you, or what the entire circle is beholden to for reviving them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T09:44:57-07:00","id":954989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=954984#post954984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pah. That's for soft players. What kind of drama or sense of the risk does the game have then? No, if the players screw up, the dice roll as they do, maybe the players die.</div> </div> </div> </div>Enh. Death is about the least interesting thing you can do to PCs. It ends their suffering. (Well, that was my Call of Cthulhu GMing philosophy, anyway, and I don't see why I should be less hardcore with my players in other games.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/978-iozz-sothoth","name":"Iozz-Sothoth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T10:41:28-07:00","id":955018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=954986#post954986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What happens while you're incapacitated, what the active characters need to do to revive you, or what the entire circle is beholden to for reviving them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, that's one thing that irritates me in 3rd ed. How serious is that dying supposed to be? I mean, is a bandage enough to save them? Serious surgery? Magic only? No idea. It's very vague.<br /> 2nd ed had a medicine difficulty to save them (5+the number of levels over incap they'd taken) which seemed a reasonable system (though I'd knock it down to maybe 3+levels over incap).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T10:45:52-07:00","id":955020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iozz-Sothoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=954989#post954989\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Enh. Death is about the least interesting thing you can do to PCs. It ends their suffering. (Well, that was my Call of Cthulhu GMing philosophy, anyway, and I don't see why I should be less hardcore with my players in other games.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I confess, I have occasionally considered &quot;should I have these bad guys fudge their rolls/make stupid decisions/decide that beating up was enough&quot; with some characters, because either a)I liked the characters, b)them dying just means a new character who's not invested in the current plot turns up to replace the old character who knew what was going on, or c)that player has a habit of making awkward characters, and this character is the least awkward they've made for a while.<br /> I mean, new characters have the same amount of XP as old ones, so...<br /> But that seems kind of cheap.<br /> <br /> But... frankly, since not one of the PCs in my 3rd ed game have ever been sent to Incap, it doesn't seem like an issue worth considering. Might as well just play the bad guys sensibly. That way they might at least seem threatening.<br /> <br /> One thing I really like about 3rd ed (and this is a house rule I considered making even before 3rd ed came out) is that you can not die by losing an eye, limb, etc.<br /> My ideal for when the party get ambushed by the Wyld Hunt is not that the Dragonblood kill one or two of the PCs (because that only traumatises the PCs and then new ones turn up) but that they cripple a couple, chopping off their arms or something. Then the PCs will think &quot;wow, the Wyld Hunt are serious business, we should try to outwit them so that doesn't happen again&quot; but not actually end up with half a party of new PCs who have no idea what the plot is and don't get on well with the old PCs.<br /> <br /> (Because once the PCs killed two of their own number, and a new player joined, so the 4 old PCs were joined by 3 new PCs, and they did not gel well. Also, the plot I was planning fell apart because the character it was based around was gone.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 08-21-2016, 01:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T12:00:13-07:00","id":955055,"title":"","content":"In terms of 3e vs 2e strictly, I'll say this. I said that I'd rather do all of Alchemicals in a 3e conversion than ever touch a 2e game ever again. I was called out on it. I went through with my promise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T12:09:38-07:00","id":955063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=954960#post954960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Asides, it takes about 5 minutes to make a new character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bwahahahahahaha HAHAHAHAHAHA!<br /> <br /> No.<br /> <br /> Not really going to argue your point (suffice it to say I disagree, but I don't care what you do at your table, so more power to you), but the idea of my players creating a character in that amount of time seems more than ludicrous to me.<br /> <br /> Hell, the idea of <b>me</b> creating a character in 5 minutes in Ex3 seems ludicrous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ultimate Jade-Screened Exalted Scholar, Savant of the Immaculate Texts, No Moon Scholar<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1304239-my-next-campaign-tdhr-peach\" target=\"_blank\">THDR : Future Dragon-Blooded campaign</a>, and other links.<br /> If you like Ex3, you can support <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/holdenshearer\" target=\"_blank\">Holden</a> on Patreon!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/541-letipex","name":"LeTipex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"902"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T12:57:33-07:00","id":955109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LeTipex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=955063#post955063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bwahahahahahaha HAHAHAHAHAHA!<br /> <br /> No.<br /> <br /> Not really going to argue your point (suffice it to say I disagree, but I don't care what you do at your table, so more power to you), but the idea of my players creating a character in that amount of time seems more than ludicrous to me.<br /> <br /> Hell, the idea of <b>me</b> creating a character in 5 minutes in Ex3 seems ludicrous.</div> </div> </div> </div>The idea of taking less than fifty minutes to create an Exalted character is hilarious unless you basically know the charmtrees by heart. Unless you just make Hotrek, the suspiciously similar son of the just deceased Gotrek.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1793-drascin","name":"Drascin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"400"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T13:07:56-07:00","id":955115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Drascin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=955109#post955109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless you just make Hotrek, the suspiciously similar son of the just deceased Gotrek.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIndeed, the point at which you're letting the player stick around by the sudden introduction of a new character who is possibly built up to a similar level of progression with everybody else is already a point at which one is conceding the point of how awkward it is to permanently remove the character of somebody who wants to continue playing.<br /> <br /> One is adding an unnecessary middle stage, at the same time as the parts about bringing a certain narrative careening to an abrupt and unsatisfactory halt.<br /> <br /> My main interest in these kinds of things is in using a character as a means of exploring the world and/or guiding them through a narrative arc, in which case something like the loss of all health levels has a higher priority as being a source of complications or something that affects which branch down the storyline things go, rather than denoting failure in a competitive entry.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T13:40:34-07:00","id":955144,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'd be pretty fucked in my seafaring game if a bad roll just outright killed Barbus or Misu today. About half the plates I've got spinning are kept such by them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T16:45:02-07:00","id":955285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=955020#post955020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, new characters have the same amount of XP as old ones, so...</div> </div> </div> </div>If you do things that way, well, sure, you don't have character death as a full-fledged game element anymore, so why keep it as a story element?<br /> <br /> If, on the other hand, new-to-the-player replacement characters are standard <i>new characters</i>, with zero XP like other new characters, well, the easy way to integrate them in Exalted is have them be the reincarnation of the dead character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T17:16:49-07:00","id":955307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=955285#post955285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you do things that way, well, sure, you don't have character death as a full-fledged game element anymore, so why keep it as a story element?<br /> <br /> If, on the other hand, new-to-the-player replacement characters are standard <i>new characters</i>, with zero XP like other new characters, well, the easy way to integrate them in Exalted is have them be the reincarnation of the dead character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending how far along the campaign is going this would really demotivate the player.<br /> <br /> I know I've left my fair share of games because of this in my young days. Now I only play with people whose views of and for the game align with mine.<br /> <br /> While random death is still possible in our games, it is very rare (hasn't happened yet in our Ex3 games). And if it does happen we will not make one of our friends play a 0xp character in a 120xp game.<br /> <br /> What we did in the past is have the new character be made with half xp/level/whatever and give them double until they catch up. So death still has some mechanic effect, but is not something that will basically make you a chump for the rest of your time at that table, who the hell deals with that? Certainly not me and mine.<br /> <br /> But hey, we also do group beats in CofD, so maybe we're just too softcore! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T17:38:18-07:00","id":955318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LeTipex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=955063#post955063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bwahahahahahaha HAHAHAHAHAHA!<br /> <br /> No.<br /> <br /> Not really going to argue your point (suffice it to say I disagree, but I don't care what you do at your table, so more power to you), but the idea of my players creating a character in that amount of time seems more than ludicrous to me.<br /> <br /> Hell, the idea of <b>me</b> creating a character in 5 minutes in Ex3 seems ludicrous.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1) What Caste do I want to play? What &quot;theme&quot; do I want my character to serve? Instantly divide up Attribute dots, and generally plan out Ability dots, based on that alone.<br /> 2) Hammer out Ability dots, choose Merits based on Theme.<br /> 3) Look at and spend Bonus Points based on theme and gap in spread.<br /> 4) Plan out Charms, after buying the near-standard Ox-Body.<br /> <br /> Of those, Charms takes the longest. Even then, I built a pretty standard entry-level Dawn in about 30 minutes, which is about 30 minutes less than it would take me to build a D&amp;D character.<br /> <br /> Finally, the absolute pain-in-the-ass level of book-flipping Charms exists as is one of the definitive reasons my group and I play mortals. Without Charms, building a mortal character takes, almost literally, 5 minutes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T17:42:48-07:00","id":955323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=955285#post955285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you do things that way, well, sure, you don't have character death as a full-fledged game element anymore, so why keep it as a story element?<br /> <br /> If, on the other hand, new-to-the-player replacement characters are standard <i>new characters</i>, with zero XP like other new characters, well, the easy way to integrate them in Exalted is have them be the reincarnation of the dead character.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've seen people simply quit playing after a character death when groups have harsh death penalties like this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T18:13:56-07:00","id":955339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=955318#post955318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> 1) What Caste do I want to play? What &quot;theme&quot; do I want my character to serve? Instantly divide up Attribute dots, and generally plan out Ability dots, based on that alone.<br /> 2) Hammer out Ability dots, choose Merits based on Theme.<br /> 3) Look at and spend Bonus Points based on theme and gap in spread.<br /> 4) Plan out Charms, after buying the near-standard Ox-Body.<br /> <br /> Of those, Charms takes the longest. Even then, I built a pretty standard entry-level Dawn in about 30 minutes, which is about 30 minutes less than it would take me to build a D&amp;D character.<br /> <br /> Finally, the absolute pain-in-the-ass level of book-flipping Charms exists as is one of the definitive reasons my group and I play mortals. Without Charms, building a mortal character takes, almost literally, 5 minutes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, full disclaimer, it is your table and you do what you want, but if a player came to my table with a character that was just stats and charms and a vague theme I'd have to stop, sit them down and say, &quot;So who is your character exactly&quot; before anything else could happen. I wouldn't allow a character who just fell out of a sky in a D&amp;D game, and I sure would not allow it in a game that is incredibly player-driven like Exalted. To that regard, i'm also wondering how many STs feel that the game is &quot;my story&quot; as you put it, and not the story of the characters. It just sounds like a game that I would really not want to play in, and a philosophy that would be an instant turn off for me if I sat down at that table no matter what the game was. Not saying you're wrong for doing what you feel like doing, it is just a completely alien philosophy to me, and I'm a little curious if I'm an outlier, you're an outlier, or it is more of an even spread. Probably a question for another thread.<br /> <br /> I would also say that over a very long time playing Exalted 3e now, running two separate groups and playing in a third, I have seen four people use their crippling injury ripcord. An arm, a leg, a jaw, and an eye.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, to throw my two cents in to the original subject, I think that my preference for 3e really comes from something that is best demonstrated through character concept and the way I've helped players through character creation in both editions.<br /> <br /> 2e<br /> - Pick your concept, pick your caste, pick your attributes.<br /> - Pick your abilities, make sure you pick at least one combat ability that has defensive abilities. Make sure you have a social ability.<br /> - Now you can pick the abilities that fit your concept.<br /> - First pick your perfect combat defense charms, if you don't have this you'll probably die quickly.<br /> - Pick your perfect mental defense charms, if you don't have this your character is going to get brainwashed by the first social person that comes along (but if they do come along, just sock them in the mouth because you can't social influence during combat).<br /> - Now you can pick the charms that fit your concept.<br /> - Make sure you want to fight you get an artifact, pretty much necessary. They're weapons with bigger stats.<br /> - Pick your virtues. Make sure you put a lot in Conviction and Valor.<br /> <br /> 3e<br /> - Here are the flavors of what the different charms do, you're a solar so you get a supernal which kind of is the definition of your myths for the most part.<br /> - Pick your caste and concept, pick your attributes, pick your abilities. Raise your supernal to five with bonus points.<br /> - Pick your charms.<br /> - Pick your intimacies, there's no real limit to how many you take, but these define what your character cares about so they're pretty cool. No, they don't cost anything extra.<br /> <br /> I know I've simplified them both quite a bit, but the point is that there is a lot more you have to do in 2e to make your character viable before you can actually build your character. Until you get perfect defenses and buy up enough dots in the right virtues your character isn't really viable in gameplay for 2e. In 3e a suboptimal build is an entirely viable and playable character, I've seen characters both with 0 combat abilities and with 0 social abilities and they don't instantly end up dead or playing a character that wasn't the one they designed. You're not limited so much by what the system makes you do, but really more free to explore what you want to do and to build the character that you actually wanted to build when that idea popped into your head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/944864-abyssals-in-death-s-dream-kingdom-homebrew-wip-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals</a><br /> <br /> My attempt at a homebrew for Abyssals, focusing on unique charms.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11602-five_gee","name":"Five_Gee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T18:36:11-07:00","id":955343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five_Gee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=955339#post955339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> -snip-<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Let me preface this by stating the following:<br /> <br /> Every single post I have made in this thread concerns character death. That is my main focus.<br /> <br /> To that end, the line &quot; my story, not the characters&quot; means that, while the plot of the campaign is heavily influenced by the actions of the characters, I am not going to change the outcome of an encounter, nor shift around the plot, merely to avoid character death. <br /> <br /> That's ...... that's it. I don't tiptoe around the issue. My games are lethal, and if you &quot;make a mistake&quot;; do something foolish in combat, piss off the wrong people, etc, you are going to get severely hurt, probably killed. After that, I explain how I am going to run my games, and the base mechanics behind combat (Onslaught Penalties are a big one, alongside Defend Other, as well as the various weapon-related abilties), and how to interact with others in in-game social situations.<br /> <br /> There are posters on this forum that apparently actively avoid that, character death that is.. I can't understand why. I have played characters that have died before, and while it got me irritated, I wasn't mad at the game, I wasn't mad at the dice. I was irritated with myself, for choosing to undertake what later ended up being a lethal mistake.<br /> <br /> For example: my long-time D&amp;D character ended up getting killed by some mooks, as he got surrounded/flanked and proceeded to get absolutely murdered by flanking bonuses and Aid Another actions. I didn't quit the game, but thought to myself, &quot; Wow, that was pretty damn stupid of me. I deserved to die&quot;. I have had players who's characters have died as well, as as soon as I explained <u>why</u> they died ( usually what they &quot;did wrong&quot; and the mechanics behind it), they almost instantly understood, and started &quot;thinking&quot; about what to do better next time.<br /> <br /> I haven't had a player leave due to character death in several years.<br /> <br /> People who, to be crass, get &quot;all butthurt&quot; when their character dies do not sound like people I want to play with, either as a player or as a DM<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T18:54:43-07:00","id":955352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=955343#post955343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To that end, the line &quot; my story, not the characters&quot; means that, while the plot of the campaign is heavily influenced by the actions of the characters, I am not going to change the outcome of an encounter, nor shift around the plot, merely to avoid character death.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>To my interpretation, the phrase with the particular emphasis placed on &quot;my&quot; meant something a whole lot different on my reading. Very different connotation to me. I get the idea of not changing encounters or results to favor anyone, what happens happens, after all. Sorry for misinterpreting, I get your stance, while I may not wholly agree with it in every single circumstance. People have fun different ways, and sometimes a story really suffers for a character's death, and sometimes it doesn't, and sometimes it is even improved by it. I prefer to maintain some flexibility and shoot for what is most fun for me and the people at my table, and on occasion that is a saving grace. There are times when death is purely chance and bad luck and it is not a satisfying addition to the narrative of the story. I'd say in Exalted that death comes up rarely enough that I can't, with certainty, say whether that type of death is more common or whether a death that is a good addition to the story is more common.<br /> <br /> With all that said, if a player died, made a character and tried to come back all in that same session I would almost certainly not allow it. For one I would need to, in most cases, think of a good way to introduce the character. Secondly, I would really be hard pressed to believe that was a character built over that short a period of time was actually fully developed and attached to the setting in a meaningful way.<br /> <br /> Now if a player had a backup character ready because they knew for certain their character was on a collision path with death? Well that is a whole other situation, especially if they've informed me of the backup character and I've had time to think on it and how it is best introduced.<br /> <br /> But that is me, and as with anything in life, your mileage may vary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/944864-abyssals-in-death-s-dream-kingdom-homebrew-wip-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals</a><br /> <br /> My attempt at a homebrew for Abyssals, focusing on unique charms.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11602-five_gee","name":"Five_Gee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11602_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T02:29:10-07:00","id":955485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=955285#post955285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you do things that way, well, sure, you don't have character death as a full-fledged game element anymore, so why keep it as a story element?<br /> <br /> If, on the other hand, new-to-the-player replacement characters are standard <i>new characters</i>, with zero XP like other new characters, well, the easy way to integrate them in Exalted is have them be the reincarnation of the dead character.</div> </div> </div> </div>XP isn't the measure of a character in the party, the social interactions, backstory and relationships are. I play in that group and Wizard now does the same thing I have for years with XP, that everyone gets the same, it solves a number of issues. But the big one for me is that XP is not the reward for playing, playing is. Just because somebody can't make a session doesn't mean that the character isn't doing things and that player deserves to be down xp, because that can effect their enjoyment in terms of how much they can do and make my job difficult in formulating challenges for them if people have different xp levels.<br /> <br /> That in my expirence is a way to have one player with dead characters much more often than other people, which isn't really all that fun. <br /> <br /> Having people be the reincarnation of a character can be fine if the player is into that, if not then it is normally under explored. Again in my expirence past exaltation don't grab all that many people.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2325-builder","name":"Builder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T08:41:57-07:00","id":955609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Five_Gee</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=955339#post955339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...and I'm a little curious if I'm an outlier, you're an outlier, or it is more of an even spread...</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u00b4m pretty sure our friend there is the outlier. I\u00b4m trying to picture a first session with this table.<br /> <br /> <b>New Guy:</b> Heya people! Whats up?! Since its my first time playing with y\u00b4all I brought the whiskey and weed! Lets do this!<br /> <br /> <b>GM:</b> This game is seriouz buzinezz. We expect you to play a certain way.<br /> <br /> <b>New Guy:</b> ... Okay. (Puts away weed and whiskey)<br /> <br /> <b>GM:</b> If you die its because you\u00b4re stupid. Don\u00b4t worry though I\u00b4ll tell you how stupid you were so you can be less stupid next time.<br /> <br /> <b>Old Timer:</b> Isn\u00b4t he such a nice guy?! (crazy eyed half smile)<br /> <br /> <b>New Guy:</b> ...Yeah...<br /> <br /> <b>GM:</b> One more thing, my main rule is: The dice fall where they may! (Mustache twirling...)<br /> <br /> <b>Old Timer 2:</b> Thats how we roll! (twicth)<br /> <br /> <b>New Guy:</b> I guess thats cool... At least we get to see the results of our action! I love rolling the dice and the anticipation of watching them show the results!<br /> <br /> <b>GM:</b> I roll all the dice. And they all fall behind my screen. The results are what I tell you they are.<br /> <br /> <b>New Guy (backing away):</b> I... ummm... Forgot the Mountain Dew in the car! Let me get it real quick!<br /> <br /> <b>Psychos:</b> GO GET THE DEW!!!!<br /> <br /> <b>New Guy leaves to never come back</b>.<br /> <br /> lol<br /> <br /> Seriously though, this has all the hallmarks of an abusive relationship. You\u00b4re supposed to behave a certain way, if you don\u00b4t you get called names. But don\u00b4t worry little by little he\u00b4ll teach you what he expects of you. And you are never in control, what he says is what goes, reality doesn\u00b4t matter, you just have to trust him on this...<br /> <br /> Scary shit.<br /> <br /> I\u00b4ll be the butthurt guy that leaves before I\u00b4m one of the brain damaged that stay anyday.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T08:50:37-07:00","id":955618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=955285#post955285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you do things that way, well, sure, you don't have character death as a full-fledged game element anymore, so why keep it as a story element?<br /> <br /> If, on the other hand, new-to-the-player replacement characters are standard <i>new characters</i>, with zero XP like other new characters, well, the easy way to integrate them in Exalted is have them be the reincarnation of the dead character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ugh, that just means the new character will die like a chump, and then his replacement will die like a chump, and his replacement will die like a chump...<br /> I played that character. It was frustrating that me and one other guy had played 6 or 7 characters while other people were on their first character, because we died every 2-3 combats while others found it easy.<br /> <br /> That, and Builder talking to me about it, made me decide to give new characters the same xp, approximately. They don't necessarily have exactly the same, perhaps slightly less, (for example, they might have 350 while everyone else has 370, or something), especially as brand-new characters tend to be better built than characters who earned that xp organically, but it's in the same ball-park.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T08:54:31-07:00","id":955623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Builder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=955485#post955485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> XP isn't the measure of a character in the party, the social interactions, backstory and relationships are. I play in that group and Wizard now does the same thing I have for years with XP, that everyone gets the same, it solves a number of issues. But the big one for me is that XP is not the reward for playing, playing is. Just because somebody can't make a session doesn't mean that the character isn't doing things and that player deserves to be down xp, because that can effect their enjoyment in terms of how much they can do and make my job difficult in formulating challenges for them if people have different xp levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I think this is an important point. I used to not give people xp when they missed sessions, but that just meant that people who couldn't come so much would come back to find their character weak compared to everyone else,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Having people be the reincarnation of a character can be fine if the player is into that, if not then it is normally under explored. Again in my expirence past exaltation don't grab all that many people. </div> </div> </div>I enjoy doing it, and once played a game where I played a character, then her reincarnation, then his reincarnation. But that doesn't necessarily require having less XP: you can make characters who had a reason to have more xp spent on some stuff (like, they were a martial artist before exalting), or have a character who starts with 100 unspent xp, and spends it rapidly to &quot;catch up&quot; with the more experienced players.<br /> <br /> (I'm actually playing a character right now who has a few hundred unspent xp, so he's going to learn kung-fu and spells from the other characters)<br /> <br /> Anyway, you're right. Most people don't care that much about it.<br /> For one thing, because they want to play a different caste.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T09:16:27-07:00","id":955634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=955609#post955609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u00b4m pretty sure our friend there is the outlier. I\u00b4m trying to picture a first session with this table.<br /> <br /> (Snip)<br /> <br /> Seriously though, this has all the hallmarks of an abusive relationship. You\u00b4re supposed to behave a certain way, if you don\u00b4t you get called names. But don\u00b4t worry little by little he\u00b4ll teach you what he expects of you. And you are never in control, what he says is what goes, reality doesn\u00b4t matter, you just have to trust him on this...<br /> <br /> Scary shit.<br /> <br /> I\u00b4ll be the butthurt guy that leaves before I\u00b4m one of the brain damaged that stay anyday.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's kind of being a bit ridiculous, don't you think? I get where he's coming from.<br /> I like to know that I've achieved something difficult and challenging, even if it was partly because of luck, not that the STs gone easy and &quot;let&quot; me succeed. I don't expect STs to fudge dice for me. The bad luck and bad rolls make the good ones sweeter.<br /> (I also don't like it when the ST fudges things to make the story interesting by making me fail of course)<br /> I like to imagine the roleplaying world is one where people achieve things by themselves, not by the will of a capricious and all-powerful God, even for the sake of a good story.<br /> <br /> A good ST sets things up so that it's very unlikely that good or bad rolls will screw up the plot.<br /> (3rd ed makes this make much easier than 2nd ed, when sudden random death was certainly feasible)<br /> <br /> Personally, I think it's hilarious fun almost every time my character dies, if it's due to bad luck or stupidity.<br /> The only times I'd be peeved is when the ST isn't running things in a &quot;realistic&quot; (from the perspective of the game-world, which might be magical or whatever) way and that got me killed (like the bad guys automatically know the players' plans) or when stupid players got me killed because they're arsing around (like when my DB got back-handed in the face with a grand goremaul by another DB because he didn't like the same kind of music, because the other player forgot that we were playing 2nd and thus being hit with a goremaul when you're an Essence 2 Dragonblood bureaucrat is something that will definitely kill you).<br /> But the rest of the time, I always find it very amusing.<br /> <br /> I've also refused, twice, to let STs retcon my character's death so that they were actually alive, because I felt it would harm the versimilitude and sense of risk of the game.<br /> <br /> And if my character dies doing something amazing and awesome and heroic... that's even better! Like when my Air Aspect grappled Walker in Darkness for 3 rounds while the other PCs put a ton of damage on him. Then he punched her head clean off, but it was awesome!<br /> <br /> Now, I'm well aware that not everyone has the same opinion as me (which is why none of the PCs in my game have died), and a good ST should think about the kind of game the players want.<br /> But I think you're being a bit ridiculous in the way you're presenting Boston123. I don't think players who choose to play his game are &quot;brain-damaged.&quot; I'd have no problem with this kind of ST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 08-22-2016, 12:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T09:22:04-07:00","id":955642,"title":"","content":"So, back to 3rd ed vs 2nd ed...<br /> 3rd ed is much easier for the ST to not actually kill people by accident. That was an issue in 2nd ed. Though I mostly saw players kill each other by accident, rather than the ST (let's see... 3 times? 3 times is what I remember off the top of my head, but there was probably more times).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T09:31:09-07:00","id":955645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=955634#post955634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's kind of being a bit ridiculous, don't you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is meant to be over the top and satiric.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=955634#post955634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get where he's coming from.<br /> I like to know that I've achieved something difficult and challenging, even if it was partly because of luck, not that the STs gone easy and &quot;let&quot; me succeed. I don't expect STs to fudge dice for me. The bad luck and bad rolls make the good ones sweeter.<br /> (I also don't like it when the ST fudges things to make the story interesting by making me fail of course)<br /> I like to imagine the roleplaying world is one where people achieve things by themselves, not by the will of a capricious and all-powerful God, even for the sake of a good story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, but you will never know if it is luck or just the control freak telling you what happens so the story goes the way he wants. You don\u00b4t roll (seriously? has anyone else ever played with a GM that rolls all dice? in storyteller, of all games?) or get to see the results of the dice here, rmember. You will never know if he is fudging to kill or save you. And remember if you die, it wasn\u00b4t bad luck. You\u00b4re just stupid. And if you leave you\u00b4re butthurt.<br /> <br /> You are playing the story of a capricious all-powerful God. <b>His</b> story, by his own words.<br /> <br /> LOL. Hilarious. Sad thing is some people will endure this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=955634#post955634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A good ST sets things up so that it's very unlikely that good or bad rolls will screw up the plot.<br /> (3rd ed makes this make much easier than 2nd ed, when sudden random death was certainly feasible)</div> </div> </div> </div>Which isn\u00b4t what our friend said he was doing. You must know what he considers safe to attempt something. Or else you die. Because you\u00b4re stupid. Don\u00b4t worry though, our friend there will teach you how to be less stupid, so next time you don\u00b4t mess up and he has to kill your character again. You will learn eventually.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=955634#post955634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I think it's hilarious fun almost every time my character dies, if it's due to bad luck or stupidity.<br /> The only times I'd be peeved is when the ST isn't running things in a &quot;realistic&quot; (from the perspective of the game-world, which might be magical or whatever) way and that got me killed (like the bad guys automatically know the players' plans) or when stupid players got me killed because they're arsing around (like when my DB got back-handed in the face with a grand goremaul by another DB because he didn't like the same kind of music, because the other player forgot that we were playing 2nd and thus being hit with a goremaul when you're an Essence 2 Dragonblood bureaucrat is something that will definitely kill you).<br /> But the rest of the time, I always find it very amusing.<br /> <br /> And if my character dies doing something amazing and awesome and heroic... that's even better! Like when my Air Aspect grappled Walker in Darkness for 3 rounds while the other PCs put a ton of damage on him. Then he punched her head clean off, but it was awesome!</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, few things are as powerful in a story as a meaningful death. Meaningful is the keyword there, though.<br /> <br /> I\u00b4m not even opposed to &quot;whatever the dice say goes&quot;, but I would sure like to roll the dice and see the result!<br /> <br /> lol<br /> <br /> This is so bad, I laugh just thinking about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T09:43:53-07:00","id":955649,"title":"","content":"Oh, I didn't see that he rolls all the dice.<br /> Yeah, that's kind of lame for the players.<br /> I mean, maybe some stuff that they shouldn't know if they succeeded or not (like, say, rolls to see if someone's lying), but it's kind of dull if people don't get to roll themselves.<br /> <br /> (I play over skype, so I don't even know what my players rolled, they could be lying for all I know)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T11:25:42-07:00","id":955733,"title":"","content":"Years and years ago I played with an AD&amp;D group that, if your character died and you weren't rezzed, you have to make a new character and start at level 1. It sure was a blast when everyone else in the group was between levels 12-14 and you were the level 1 wizard. <br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, the Beholder looks at you. You're dead.&quot; <br /> <br /> You'd have to spend the next several sessions hiding behind the other players and not doing anything to attract attention (because you'd be one shot by anything that glanced in your direction) while the rest of the group power-leveled you. <br /> <br /> They found it fun, I guess. Or maybe they had always just played that way and it had never occurred to them to play differently. I know I didn't enjoy it.<br /> <br /> I think there's a huge line between &quot;Character death needs to be meaningful&quot; and, &quot;Character death needs to be punishing.&quot; There are lots of ways to make it meaningful without punishing the player (or the ST as is often the case when a PC dies and half his story plots and hooks suddenly evaporate).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T14:29:08-07:00","id":955892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=955609#post955609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> -snip-<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Cute.<br /> <br /> I keep the character sheets because having to explain what is going on for the third time because you happened to be idly reading through your character sheet isn't just annoying for me, it is annoying for the rest of the group. I do give the players a list of their attacks, social stuff, and skills and the like, so they aren't in the dark<br /> <br /> I roll the dice for two reasons. 1) It adds quite a bit of verisimilitude when you can't look at your character sheet and go, &quot; Oh, I've got 30hp left, I'm good.&quot; Instead, you actually have to listen to me describe what is going on, what is happening to the character. Instead of instantly knowing if you fail or succeed (and not even paying attention to the rest of the scene), instead you actually have to ....... pay attention to how I describe it. 2) Speed. I can throw as many dice out as I need to, while some players like to throw out a single die at a time, or some other time-wasting action.<br /> It just makes it easier for me. <br /> <br /> &quot;doing stupid things&quot; is straight from the mechanics. In D&amp;D, a &quot;stupid thing&quot; would be getting flanked. In Exalted, a &quot;stupid thing&quot; would be getting attacked by more than one opponent and letting the Onslaught Penalties pile up. Or, forgetting that Gambits exist, and refuse to help out your allies in combat. Or, forgetting that Full Defense is a thing. Or, <u>failing to realize that the current situation is above their head</u>, and refusing to actually back out of combat or a bad social situation.<br /> <br /> Which is why we take, basically, the entire first gaming session and read through the mechanics. I make sure everyone understands them. After that, you dying due to not understanding how the mechanics get implemented is basically your fault...... which is why I call said deaths &quot;stupid&quot;.<br /> <br /> While I certainly expect a lot from my players, they expect even more from me. They tell me what they want to play. So far, we have done Vikings, Warring-States-style Hundred Kingdoms (arguably the best), a recreation of the Odyssey, and right now I am working on a &quot;Mists of Avalon&quot; style campaign. All at my players urgings and suggestions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11892-boston123","name":"Boston123","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T15:20:34-07:00","id":955927,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=955892#post955892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cute.<br /> ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Suffice to say that your playstyle is a huge turn off for me. I like having my sheet and rolling my dice. I can understand a secret roll here and there, but I like the ST to roll where people can see too. They can already make up any stats/pool they want, so why hide the results? I don\u00b4t even have a ST screen, when I ST all rolls are visible. I have a practice to ask for perception/awareness rolls randomly, sometimes when people succeed I just describe a setting detail they would have missed. They never know if they missed an assassin in the shadows or the merchant skimping on that lady\u00b4s basket of apples. If they fail a lie detection, they just can\u00b4t tell if it is true or false, if they make it they can.<br /> <br /> I don\u00b4t play games where one mistake will set you back forever. This ain\u00b4t real life, I don\u00b4t want to deal with that on my recreational time.<br /> <br /> It is great that you and yours have fun. And if you had exposed your opinions without demeaning others I don\u00b4t believe anyone would mock you.<br /> <br /> If you think yourself entitled to label me &quot;butthurt&quot;, don\u00b4t mind me tagging you &quot;seriouz gamez control freak&quot;. Goose and gander.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T17:03:27-07:00","id":955995,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=955892#post955892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Cute.<br /> <br /> I keep the character sheets because having to explain what is going on for the third time because you happened to be idly reading through your character sheet isn't just annoying for me, it is annoying for the rest of the group. I do give the players a list of their attacks, social stuff, and skills and the like, so they aren't in the dark<br /> <br /> I roll the dice for two reasons. 1) It adds quite a bit of verisimilitude when you can't look at your character sheet and go, &quot; Oh, I've got 30hp left, I'm good.&quot; Instead, you actually have to listen to me describe what is going on, what is happening to the character. Instead of instantly knowing if you fail or succeed (and not even paying attention to the rest of the scene), instead you actually have to ....... pay attention to how I describe it. 2) Speed. I can throw as many dice out as I need to, while some players like to throw out a single die at a time, or some other time-wasting action.<br /> It just makes it easier for me.<br /> <br /> &quot;doing stupid things&quot; is straight from the mechanics. In D&amp;D, a &quot;stupid thing&quot; would be getting flanked. In Exalted, a &quot;stupid thing&quot; would be getting attacked by more than one opponent and letting the Onslaught Penalties pile up. Or, forgetting that Gambits exist, and refuse to help out your allies in combat. Or, forgetting that Full Defense is a thing. Or, <u>failing to realize that the current situation is above their head</u>, and refusing to actually back out of combat or a bad social situation.<br /> <br /> Which is why we take, basically, the entire first gaming session and read through the mechanics. I make sure everyone understands them. After that, you dying due to not understanding how the mechanics get implemented is basically your fault...... which is why I call said deaths &quot;stupid&quot;.<br /> <br /> While I certainly expect a lot from my players, they expect even more from me. They tell me what they want to play. So far, we have done Vikings, Warring-States-style Hundred Kingdoms (arguably the best), a recreation of the Odyssey, and right now I am working on a &quot;Mists of Avalon&quot; style campaign. All at my players urgings and suggestions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find it's best to keep in mind that <b>gaming-as-escapism</b> is the dominant form of play for Exalted, at least, Exalted messageboard denizens. Gaming-as-survival, Combat-as-War, Gaming-as-Challenge are not the default paradigms and that is helpful to remember when discussing Exalted online. FWIW, I prefer my gaming much like yours, but that doesn't get you any sympathy here. It just doesn't pay to get into those kinds of playstyle arguments here. Trust me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T17:41:13-07:00","id":956018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=955307#post955307\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depending how far along the campaign is going this would really demotivate the player.</div> </div> </div> </div>This statement, of course, packages an assumption about campaigns having a strong, play-relevant time progression, which would itself encourage one to restrict opportunities for character death.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=955323#post955323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've seen people simply quit playing after a character death when groups have harsh death penalties like this.</div> </div> </div> </div>And? People quitting a game because it's not to their taste does not actually indicate anything wrong with a given approach, unless your position is that every single group's game is obligated to appeal to every single possible gamer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Builder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=955485#post955485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">XP isn't the measure of a character in the party, the social interactions, backstory and relationships are</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. If that's your viewpoint, then you are already well on your way to limiting character death to narrative reasons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=955618#post955618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ugh, that just means the new character will die like a chump, and then his replacement will die like a chump, and his replacement will die like a chump...</div> </div> </div> </div>Only under an implicit assumption about how a campaign handles threat levels that largely moves one in the direction of restricting death to start with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T17:46:45-07:00","id":956024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=956018#post956018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This statement, of course, packages an assumption about campaigns having a strong, play-relevant time progression, which would itself encourage one to restrict opportunities for character death.<br /> <br /> ...</div> </div> </div> </div>That &quot;would&quot; should really be a &quot;could&quot;. Either way, I'm not getting your point. Care to elaborate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T17:49:29-07:00","id":956028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boston123</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=955892#post955892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cute.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I understand the desire to be serious with your games. I understand the desire to have your players pay attention, and the desire to have more serious &quot;Actions have consequences and if you fuck up you die&quot;. It's not my cup of tea, but I <i>understand</i> it.<br /> <br /> What I <i>don't</i> understand is the overly draconian methods you seem to use. And yeah, I think &quot;I have all the character sheets, I roll all the dice, and it's hidden&quot; <i>is</i> overly draconian. Because there's using a firm hand, and there's &quot;I run all the numbers and do all the rolls for you&quot;, which... At that point, you're almost doing the entire game by yourself with an audience crying out suggestions for the people you're rolling for.<br /> <br /> I can also say that &quot;People missing what I'm saying because they're busy reading their character sheet&quot; is something I have literally never had happen before. If it does at your table, then maybe you should talk to the player. Players DO get distracted sometimes, and at that point I find a slightly raised voice (&quot;Focus! Thank you. Now-&quot;) or a swift knock on the tabletop with my knuckles gets their attention, to prevent someone from having to repeat themselves.<br /> <br /> Granted, apparently your players are okay with it. All I know is that if it were me, the SECOND you said &quot;I'm keeping your character sheet, and I'm rolling for you&quot; I'd just leave and never look back.<br /> <br /> Because, and I won't say that your players are wrong for having fun, but I will say that <b>I literally cannot comprehend someone enjoying the way you run your games</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T18:22:30-07:00","id":956047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=956018#post956018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And? People quitting a game because it's not to their taste does not actually indicate anything wrong with a given approach, unless your position is that every single group's game is obligated to appeal to every single possible gamer.</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that Joe might decide to quit the game if the punishment for death is too severe is probably worth keeping mind when coming up with how you plan to handle character death. Well, at least if you give a shit about Joe and care whether he shows up at your table each week or not. If you don't care, then of course it doesn't matter at all.<br /> <br /> If everyone in the group is on board with punishing death mechanics and starting over from zero when their character dies, then go for it. But if some people in the group aren't, then it's probably in the ST's best interest to consider their opinions. At the end of the day, roleplaying is a group entertainment exercise and if someone is having so little fun they decide to stop showing up, then I would imagine there was a failure somewhere along the way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T18:26:41-07:00","id":956048,"title":"","content":"Re: XP for new/restarting players - something I've had some success with, especially for new Exalted players joining an established game, is to give new players double or triple the XP awards you give everyone else until they catch up. (This does require tracking &quot;How much total XP does everyone have?&quot; but Ex3 requires that <i>anyway</i>.)<br /> <br /> The benefit there is that it doesn't bury a new player under the <i>mountains</i> of chargen decisions they'll have if the party is, say, 75 regular XP (and 50 Solar XP) down the road - they catch up relatively quickly, with a chance to figure out how their character works along the way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/773992-homebrew-lunar-charms-for-3e\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew: Lunar Charms for 3e</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/833007-complete-ex3-solar-charm-rewrite\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Charm Rewrite (Complete)</a> (Now with Charm cards!)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1376-irked","name":"Irked","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T19:23:06-07:00","id":956080,"title":"","content":"Did something similar to Irked in my seafaring game with the introduction of Misu; as a new player to Exalted altogether, he had no desire to build his first character only to effectively pile two <i>more</i> characters on top.<br /> <br /> So he started at chargen, which is a lot more forgiving in Ex3 than it was in D&amp;D or even in 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T22:51:04-07:00","id":956171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=956080#post956080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So he started at chargen, which is a lot more forgiving in Ex3 than it was in D&amp;D or even in 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's also the &quot;Build a more experienced Solar&quot; sidebar, which IS a pretty nifty little thing I've used.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T02:15:51-07:00","id":956220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=955649#post955649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I didn't see that he rolls all the dice.<br /> Yeah, that's kind of lame for the players.<br /> I mean, maybe some stuff that they shouldn't know if they succeeded or not (like, say, rolls to see if someone's lying), but it's kind of dull if people don't get to roll themselves.<br /> <br /> (I play over skype, so I don't even know what my players rolled, they could be lying for all I know)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yep, we lie to you all the time, its for your own good.....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2325-builder","name":"Builder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2325_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-23T18:47:20-07:00","id":956682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=956024#post956024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That &quot;would&quot; should really be a &quot;could&quot;. Either way, I'm not getting your point. Care to elaborate?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're very obviously assuming a campaign that has one group of &quot;main character&quot; PCs, who advance in ability at approximately the same rate as a group, and who usually face encounters pre-calibrated for their power level. Those are common assumptions, but they're only assumptions -- as can be seen by the fact that they were <i>all</i> untrue of the original, pre-publication-of-D&amp;D Greyhawk and Blackmoor campaigns.<br /> <br /> With those assumptions, character death is inherently a major issue on the level of replacing one of the handful of main cast members on a TV show, and that really <i>would</i> encourage restricting opportunities for character death, along with encouraging new characters joining that group being created at about the same power level as that group, et cetera.<br /> <br /> Without those assumptions, it's rather hard to intelligibly speak about &quot;how far along&quot; a campaign is at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T07:06:44-07:00","id":956928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irked</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=956048#post956048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Re: XP for new/restarting players - something I've had some success with, especially for new Exalted players joining an established game, is to give new players double or triple the XP awards you give everyone else until they catch up. (This does require tracking &quot;How much total XP does everyone have?&quot; but Ex3 requires that <i>anyway</i>.)<br /> <br /> The benefit there is that it doesn't bury a new player under the <i>mountains</i> of chargen decisions they'll have if the party is, say, 75 regular XP (and 50 Solar XP) down the road - they catch up relatively quickly, with a chance to figure out how their character works along the way.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is a good system, though I just give them the XP and tell them they don't have to spend it all at once. Most do, but sometimes they'll only spend 1/3 of their xp or something.<br /> <br /> I recently retired my 800xp Lunar (who had multiple mutations, amnesia, and his shadow had run off to become a creepy stalker monster... he really needed to go train with some elders, learn about being a Lunar, and get tattooed), but I didn't really want to make a new 800xp Solar, especially as the game is 2nd ed (and presumably will convert to 3rd ed later).<br /> So I made a 400xp-ish ghost-blood martial artist. If he ever exalts as a Solar he'll probably have like 100xp. But I couldn't really be bothered to spend it all, and I'd rather grow the character organically.<br /> <br /> I think though, that it depends a bit on the game: in low-intensity, low-combat games, people playing much weaker characters is much more doable than in very dangerous games.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T17:54:17-07:00","id":957292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=955995#post955995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I find it's best to keep in mind that <b>gaming-as-escapism</b> is the dominant form of play for Exalted, at least, Exalted messageboard denizens. Gaming-as-survival, Combat-as-War, Gaming-as-Challenge are not the default paradigms and that is helpful to remember when discussing Exalted online. FWIW, I prefer my gaming much like yours, but that doesn't get you any sympathy here. It just doesn't pay to get into those kinds of playstyle arguments here. Trust me.</div> </div> </div> </div>For all you combat in my games are much deadlier than on his. My games could be much more challenging. <br /> <br /> And there is no way you would know because what was being discussed is what to do when a character dies. Not how often, or if they should die at all.<br /> <br /> I have no problem in killing a character who dicks around with the wrong people. Done it plenty. I just don't believe the player should be forever ( in that game's context) setback because a character died. I also let him use all his tricks and whatever he can imagine to save his hide. And have the NPCs do the same.<br /> <br /> The players can have their sheets and roll their dice, the ST can roll the dice where everyone can see and it could still be a Combat-as-War game. <br /> <br /> Who handles the sheets and roll the dice, and what happens when a character is permanently removed from the game, has no bearing on this.<br /> <br /> PS Not saying that my games are CaW or GaC, just saying that this argument has nothing to do with what was being discussed by the post you quoted. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-24T20:51:50-07:00","id":957379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=957292#post957292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For all you combat in my games are much deadlier than on his. My games could be much more challenging.<br /> <br /> And there is no way you would know because what was being discussed is what to do when a character dies. Not how often, or if they should die at all.<br /> <br /> I have no problem in killing a character who dicks around with the wrong people. Done it plenty. I just don't believe the player should be forever ( in that game's context) setback because a character died. I also let him use all his tricks and whatever he can imagine to save his hide. And have the NPCs do the same.<br /> <br /> The players can have their sheets and roll their dice, the ST can roll the dice where everyone can see and it could still be a Combat-as-War game.<br /> <br /> Who handles the sheets and roll the dice, and what happens when a character is permanently removed from the game, has no bearing on this.<br /> <br /> PS Not saying that my games are CaW or GaC, just saying that this argument has nothing to do with what was being discussed by the post you quoted.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Gaming-as-Escapism tends to believe much more in player agency mattering over most other things but this viewpoint is not an absolute. Various ranges of player agency exist across many different gaming styles, including ST rolling, as well as ST hidden information. The play-style the person in question is using is actually SUGGESTED as an advanced playstyle by the VtM Storytellers Guide revised. This might be a rare heron, but it's not a dodo.<br /> <br /> Generally, a correlation between Gaming-as-Escapism and a lack of hard consequences exists. I've never seen a game with the levers of agency over death switched on which also had hard combat consequences and hard death consequences. Anyways, all I'm trying to say here is your way of playing isn't better than his. Just different.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T04:25:10-07:00","id":957508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=957379#post957379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Gaming-as-Escapism tends to believe much more in player agency mattering over most other things but this viewpoint is not an absolute. Various ranges of player agency exist across many different gaming styles, including ST rolling, as well as ST hidden information. The play-style the person in question is using is actually SUGGESTED as an advanced playstyle by the VtM Storytellers Guide revised. This might be a rare heron, but it's not a dodo.<br /> <br /> Generally, a correlation between Gaming-as-Escapism and a lack of hard consequences exists. I've never seen a game with the levers of agency over death switched on which also had hard combat consequences and hard death consequences. Anyways, all I'm trying to say here is your way of playing isn't better than his. Just different.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don\u00b4t understand why you are relating these things directly. There could be a ST out there who keeps the sheets and makes all the rolls and runs a very game-as-escaping table. The ST could be really strict on consequences, while allowing plenty player agency.<br /> <br /> What happens to a player after a character dies has close no impact on any of this. It doesn\u00b4t have impact in verissimilitude, as we all know that if you die in war as a general, you don\u00b4t come back as a private. You\u00b4re just dead. Unless there is an argument proposing that a player should sit out a game if their character dies the level of power a character has when it is made doesn\u00b4t relly matter.<br /> <br /> Who is arguing that a playstyle is better or not? I was making a point of demonstrating that dismissive and demeaning is not a way to go about an argument, and how shitty it is to be on the receiving end of it. People enjoy saying what they want, but have trouble listening to the feedback.<br /> <br /> Are you talking about the V:tM Storyteller's Companion or Handbook? Because I skimmed both and didn't find a playstyle suggestion where the storyteller both keeps the sheets and makes all the rolls. What I did find was the suggested Troupe Style, which has an advantage of lessning the impact on the player\u00b4s game of a specific character death. Could be me just overlooking it, though.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T11:19:27-07:00","id":957727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TGUEIROS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=957508#post957508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don\u00b4t understand why you are relating these things directly. There could be a ST out there who keeps the sheets and makes all the rolls and runs a very game-as-escaping table. The ST could be really strict on consequences, while allowing plenty player agency.<br /> <br /> What happens to a player after a character dies has close no impact on any of this. It doesn\u00b4t have impact in verissimilitude, as we all know that if you die in war as a general, you don\u00b4t come back as a private. You\u00b4re just dead. Unless there is an argument proposing that a player should sit out a game if their character dies the level of power a character has when it is made doesn\u00b4t relly matter.<br /> <br /> Who is arguing that a playstyle is better or not? I was making a point of demonstrating that dismissive and demeaning is not a way to go about an argument, and how shitty it is to be on the receiving end of it. People enjoy saying what they want, but have trouble listening to the feedback.<br /> <br /> Are you talking about the V:tM Storyteller's Companion or Handbook? Because I skimmed both and didn't find a playstyle suggestion where the storyteller both keeps the sheets and makes all the rolls. What I did find was the suggested Troupe Style, which has an advantage of lessning the impact on the player\u00b4s game of a specific character death. Could be me just overlooking it, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm relating these things directly because the original point that was being made to Boston123 was that this forum tends to skew heavily to Gaming-as-Escapism, which tends to assume things like &quot;guaranteed continuity of character&quot; to be a good thing, and in some cases people act as though playing any other way is bad or wrong. I'm trying to help this guy understand this place is not friendly to discussion going against that norm. Pointing out edge cases doesn't really detract from that.<br /> <br /> In your 2nd paragraph, you are acting as though you understand 100% of the angles and points of view on character death, as though there is a correct one. There isn't. Death is a topic of wide ranging debate on what it's role should be. It is a playstyle choice. That's why it's linked to the topic at hand.<br /> <br /> The book in question is the Vampire Storytellers Guide: Revised. Might be wrong though, all those old ST guides offered interesting and alternative ways to play. The Wraith ST guide in particular even suggested telling your players to make PC's for another WoD game as mortals, then killing them, and stating &quot;ok now we're playing Wraith&quot; as a swerve. The point of pointing this out was that within a game there are a myriad of ways to be exposed to it and play it which flip some levers to promote different styles and different kinds of fun.<br /> <br /> I only chose to jump in because I ignored my own advice: Don't get into playstyle discussions on these forums. with that, I will bow out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":255,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","user":"ParanoiaCombo","date":".  Text cleanup 08-25-2016, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-26T09:21:25-07:00","id":958264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=957727#post957727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm relating these things directly because the original point that was being made to Boston123 was that this forum tends to skew heavily to Gaming-as-Escapism, which tends to assume things like &quot;guaranteed continuity of character&quot; to be a good thing, and in some cases people act as though playing any other way is bad or wrong. I'm trying to help this guy understand this place is not friendly to discussion going against that norm. Pointing out edge cases doesn't really detract from that.<br /> <br /> In your 2nd paragraph, you are acting as though you understand 100% of the angles and points of view on character death, as though there is a correct one. There isn't. Death is a topic of wide ranging debate on what it's role should be. It is a playstyle choice. That's why it's linked to the topic at hand.<br /> <br /> The book in question is the Vampire Storytellers Guide: Revised. Might be wrong though, all those old ST guides offered interesting and alternative ways to play. The Wraith ST guide in particular even suggested telling your players to make PC's for another WoD game as mortals, then killing them, and stating &quot;ok now we're playing Wraith&quot; as a swerve. The point of pointing this out was that within a game there are a myriad of ways to be exposed to it and play it which flip some levers to promote different styles and different kinds of fun.<br /> <br /> I only chose to jump in because I ignored my own advice: Don't get into playstyle discussions on these forums. with that, I will bow out.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I think you still misunderstand me, last words matter little in my opinion. So I\u00b4ll ackowledge your desinclination to discuss further and not address those points.<br /> <br /> On the tangent though, I couldn\u00b4t find a book with that name in my collection or in DriveThru\u00b4s catalogue. Only Vampire &quot;Storyteller\u00b4s&quot; from &quot;Revised Edition&quot; that I found are the Handbook and the Companion, like mentioned in my previous post. I\u00b4ll offer that this is not a petty calling on the veracity of your claim, it is just a genuine interest to read what was suggested that following that advice would accomplish.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros","name":"TGUEIROS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2746_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-27T12:29:56-07:00","id":958835,"title":"","content":"Ignore this, messed up","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":1183,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","user":"Sandact6","date":".  I forgot I posted here 08-27-2016, 04:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-25T20:47:57-07:00","id":1533153,"title":"","content":"Has someone tried bringing charms and ideas from Ex3 back to 2nd edition?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-27T03:22:39-07:00","id":1533241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=1533153#post1533153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has someone tried bringing charms and ideas from Ex3 back to 2nd edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes several, depends on what you're looking for.<br /> <br /> I've looked at.<ul><li>\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bNPCs and locations haven't been ported into the new edition and how they might be impacted by other setting changes or elements that Ex3 decided it wasn't going to use might be helpful elsewhere.</li> <li>How to beef up NPC antagonists, especially elders and third circle demons without restoring higher attributes and abilities to create a boring slog.</li> <li>Updating specific charms because I thought they were neat, mostly happens with Solar or Martial Arts charms.</li> <li>I'm writing a supplement dealing with sex and sexuality in Creation that's unburdened by the 2e approach to such things.</li> </ul><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-28T01:39:37-07:00","id":1533303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=1533241#post1533241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes several, depends on what you're looking for.<br /> <br /> I've looked at.<ul><li>\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bNPCs and locations haven't been ported into the new edition and how they might be impacted by other setting changes or elements that Ex3 decided it wasn't going to use might be helpful elsewhere.</li> <li>How to beef up NPC antagonists, especially elders and third circle demons without restoring higher attributes and abilities to create a boring slog.</li> <li>Updating specific charms because I thought they were neat, mostly happens with Solar or Martial Arts charms.</li> <li>I'm writing a supplement dealing with sex and sexuality in Creation that's unburdened by the 2e approach to such things.</li> </ul></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, you mean elements from Ex2 brought to Ex3?<br /> <br /> Cause I meant the opposite. Things like creating an Ex2 version of Single Point Shinning into the Void Style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-29T19:41:43-07:00","id":1533368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=1533153#post1533153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has someone tried bringing charms and ideas from Ex3 back to 2nd edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorcerous Workings would port back to 2e without a whole lot of trouble in my opinion.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-30T05:58:28-07:00","id":1533376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gonzo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=1533303#post1533303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, you mean elements from Ex2 brought to Ex3?<br /> <br /> Cause I meant the opposite. Things like creating an Ex2 version of Single Point Shinning into the Void Style.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, misunderstood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-11T14:01:53-07:00","id":1534048,"title":"","content":"Just to throw my 2 obals in, I would bring back the Manga strips, more of the old artifact system (with rank 4 and 5 having evocations) and how thaumaturgy worked in the old edition, Manses having 5 levels, magitech, magic and motes being creations physics, and do a better job bringing the expanded setting in line with how it was in 2nd. Also the old Anime influence is so missed, Make the setting less milque toasty, and back to how it was, a terrible place that abused and hurt people, because Creation was a broken world inherited by and ruled by broken people who are trapped in a cycle of abuse and power dynamics. <br /> God the things that chapped my inner thigh was the tinker bell magic system (it's a miracle just clap your hands there is no science) and the remodeling of the various societies to be more &quot;progressive&quot; (removing the less pleasant qualities of the various groups and cultures instead of giving the players a chance to fix it in game, its) while at the same time erasing the elements that made each group unique causing all the groups to end up kind of samey. <br /> <br /> The new evocation system, fine for high end artifacts, but a pain in the ass for the &quot;mass&quot; produced stuff used by rank and file dragon blooded or alchemicals. While saving the evocation gear for the Lostech.<br /> also the the Core book is too flipping big, it scares every prospective player, and I broke its spine with in a month of purchase/printing.<br /> I felt the guys who initially wrote 3rd did not like the 2nd edition of the games lore or metaphysics or anime/JRPG inspired roots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1435-videopete","name":"videopete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-11T15:19:48-07:00","id":1534053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>videopete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=1534048#post1534048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to throw my 2 obals in, I would bring back the Manga strips, more of the old artifact system (with rank 4 and 5 having evocations) and how thaumaturgy worked in the old edition, Manses having 5 levels, magitech, magic and motes being creations physics, and do a better job bringing the expanded setting in line with how it was in 2nd. Also the old Anime influence is so missed, Make the setting less milque toasty, and back to how it was, a terrible place that abused and hurt people, because Creation was a broken world inherited by and ruled by broken people who are trapped in a cycle of abuse and power dynamics.<br /> God the things that chapped my inner thigh was the tinker bell magic system (it's a miracle just clap your hands there is no science).</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean like the 2e diseases?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-12T18:21:28-07:00","id":1534115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=1534053#post1534053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You mean like the 2e diseases?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it's late, maybe it's cause I haven't cracked open my core book in a hot minute, but care to explain, cause my memory was that diseases were for the most part while a detailed section of the book, was essentially easily ignored as rhe the Shard of Celestial Exaltation made diseases a non issue. So unless you were playing a moral hero campaign, diseases were ignored.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1435-videopete","name":"videopete","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1435_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-12T18:56:28-07:00","id":1534116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>videopete</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=1534115#post1534115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe it's late, maybe it's cause I haven't cracked open my core book in a hot minute, but care to explain, cause my memory was that diseases were for the most part while a detailed section of the book, was essentially easily ignored as rhe the Shard of Celestial Exaltation made diseases a non issue. So unless you were playing a moral hero campaign, diseases were ignored.</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1e, diseases happened very much in line with how they occur IRL, albeit with some obviously occluded elements due to the lack of microscopy in Creation. In 2e, they were presented as having some magical superstitious bullshit causes like criminals bathing in water or curses from deities. It was quite the whiplash-inducing shift.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-23T03:42:10-07:00","id":1534580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=1534116#post1534116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In 1e, diseases happened very much in line with how they occur IRL, albeit with some obviously occluded elements due to the lack of microscopy in Creation. In 2e, they were presented as having some magical superstitious bullshit causes like criminals bathing in water or curses from deities. It was quite the whiplash-inducing shift.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always understood these 2e descriptions as how people in Creation (don't) understand diseases, rather than how they're actually supposed to work in the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-23T06:22:42-07:00","id":1534584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=1534580#post1534580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I always understood these 2e descriptions as how people in Creation (don't) understand diseases, rather than how they're actually supposed to work in the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>We never get that indication anywhere in the text. It's just partying like it's 1599.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-23T21:50:45-07:00","id":1534615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=1534584#post1534584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We never get that indication anywhere in the text. It's just partying like it's 1599.</div> </div> </div> </div>It never occurred to me that it would need to be spelled out. I saw real diseases and rules about virulence coupled with some &quot;divine punishment&quot; descriptions and automatically thought, &quot;cool, so the average person in Creation has no idea how diseases work.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-23T22:35:01-07:00","id":1534619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=1534615#post1534615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It never occurred to me that it would need to be spelled out. I saw real diseases and rules about virulence coupled with some &quot;divine punishment&quot; descriptions and automatically thought, &quot;cool, so the average person in Creation has no idea how diseases work.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is actually contra to statements that we had back in 1e, where GCG explicitly that Creation had germ theory of disease (in keeping with how the 1e core book didn't fuck around with mystical explanations for real life diseases). Anyone who can speak to disease gods can also probably discover bits and pieces of deeper information about communicable diseases, and anyone with access to First Age texts can get glimpses about what modern medical science knows.<br /> <br /> (Ever since Savage Seas, we've also known that characters can have knowledge of root causes of disease with Lore, although in that case, it's 3+ to know that scurvy can be prevented via dietary means, typically via fresh fruits and vegetables.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-24T03:52:52-07:00","id":1534625,"title":"","content":"Having argued with many antivaxxers, I'd say there is no discrepancy between the world knowing germ theory and an average person believing in mystical explanations for the diseases. But I guess people had higher hopes for humanity back when 2e corebook dropped, so that's fair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/582-morangias","name":"Morangias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1670"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-24T08:30:13-07:00","id":1534645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Morangias</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/942281-exalted-2nd-ed-vs-3rd-ed?p=1534625#post1534625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having argued with many antivaxxers, I'd say there is no discrepancy between the world knowing germ theory and an average person believing in mystical explanations for the diseases. But I guess people had higher hopes for humanity back when 2e corebook dropped, so that's fair.</div> </div> </div> </div>The two editions' disease sections have been compared against each other ever since the core book dropped for 2e back in 2006, and the one for the 2e core has always been found wanting.<br /> <br /> (Obligatory &quot;fuck I'm old&quot; post)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}